{"id":"live-dead","parent":"bug-server","ord":"a0","title":"Live view doesn't work at all — and e2e doesn't catch it","done":"2026-08-09T20:34:19-04:00","desc":"FIXED via kolu PR #2133 (the store merge stops guessing keys) plus PR #61 (pin bump and the failing-shape e2e scenarios: mid-insert, mid-delete, reorder, poisoning — asserting the id multiset).\n- Observed 2026-08-09 in real use: a write to the served directory never reaches the page without a manual reload, while the e2e liveness suite stays green\n\n**DIAGNOSED 2026-08-09** (Grok; DIAGNOSIS.md in the live-dead worktree).\n- Root cause is UPSTREAM in kolu: @kolu/surface's solid writeWrappedValue merges each stream frame with Solid reconcile(next) under the DEFAULT key 'id' — but olai's outline nodes are Located records ({file,line,node:{id,…}}) with no top-level id, so every element keys as undefined and any membership/order change mis-merges the client store: missing nodes, duplicated nodes, scrambled lines, and a poisoned store that stays wrong for all later frames until reload\n- Server, watcher, probe, bind and WS frames are all healthy (verified leg by leg; the correct frame reaches the browser)\n- A/B-verified: reconcile(next,{key:null}) or plain replacement fixes mid-insert/mid-delete/reorder\n\n**Why e2e is green:** every liveness scenario edits in exactly the shapes keyed-reconcile survives — whole-file rewrites at stable indices and end-of-file appends — never a mid-insert, mid-delete, or reorder, and never an assertion on the full id multiset.\n\n**Fix direction:** upstream PR to kolu (writeWrappedValue must not assume key 'id' for arbitrary payloads — caller-supplied key or replace policy from the stream definition), plus e2e scenarios that fail today: mid-insert, mid-delete, reorder, mid-insert-then-append poisoning, asserting the id multiset rather than eventual title text.\n\n**Upstream fix in flight 2026-08-09:** folded into the kolu-side agent's scope (branch surface-typed-lifecycle), pointed at DIAGNOSIS.md.\n- Olai still owes, once the kolu pin moves: the failing-today e2e scenarios and the pin bump","after":["live"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"no-lifecycle","parent":"bug-server","ord":"a1","title":"Stale server accepted silently — no connection indicator","done":"2026-08-09T20:34:19-04:00","desc":"Diagnosed 2026-08-09.\n- Surface is designed to address exactly this class of bug and olai doesn't use that part: packages/web/src/client/wire.ts calls connectSurface (the no-lifecycle seam) and keeps only .client, discarding the wire status accessor\n- A tab wired to a replaced/dead server just sits there looking fine: on reconnect the new process closes it with the stale-tab code, the wire retires by design (stops re-dialing, reports status 'retired'), and nothing in the UI says so\n- **Fix:** make full use of the framework — derive createServerLifecycle (or consume the status connectSurface already returns) and render a GREEN CONNECTION INDICATOR in the UI (kolu's header dot is the house pattern), with the retired state auto-reloading or showing 'server restarted — reload'\n- **Regression test (HACKING.md):** restart the scenario-owned server under an open page and assert the page recovers; assert the indicator reflects connected/disconnected/retired\n- Pairs with the connection-health pill under mobile-pwa","after":["live"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"no-lifecycle-fix","parent":"no-lifecycle","ord":"a0","title":"The fix in olai","done":"2026-08-09T20:34:19-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #61 (squash 46b3a70), reworked onto kolu #2133 before merge.\n- connection indicator (corner dot, green only when live)\n- retired-wire recovery ('server restarted — Reload' via reloadForUpdate)\n- createServerLifecycle over the status accessor (whose projection maps retired to down)\n- an identity.info surface member feeding the pid echo — which the agent proved was previously a dead gate\n- same-port server-restart e2e scenarios\n- **Decided 2026-08-09:** this PR will also adopt the upstream kolu API from no-lifecycle-upstream once it exists, in the same PR","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"no-lifecycle-upstream","parent":"no-lifecycle","ord":"a1","title":"Upstream: make the framework prevent this #upstream","done":"2026-08-09T20:31:33-04:00","desc":"Shipped as kolu PR #2133:\n- the framework owns the stale-tab handshake end to end (system/identity carries processId, the socket feeds its own echo, rejectStaleProcess deleted)\n- the retired state is a required option on connectSurface (type-level, as preferred)\n- the store merge stops inferring element keys from field names\n- The agent was briefed on the three shapes with type-level required, the self-feeding pid echo, and the projectStatus retired→down conflation\n- **What to PR:** to @kolu/surface / surface-app so a future app cannot silently ship a lifeless wire. To be fleshed out from the PR that comes out of no-lifecycle-fix (decided 2026-08-09)\n- **Preference (human, 2026-08-09):** type-level is always best — the seam should require a status/onRetired consumer at the type level instead of letting it be discarded\n- Other shapes on the table: connectSurface defaulting a retired-state handler (reloadForUpdate) unless explicitly overridden; the app shell (surfaceAppLayer) owning a built-in connection indicator\n- Context: docs/brainstorming/surface-utilization.md","after":["no-lifecycle-fix"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"live-dead-residual","parent":"bug-server","ord":"a2","title":"Live update still duplicates rows — one layer above the fixed merge","done":"2026-08-10T13:11:19-04:00","desc":"FIXED 2026-08-10, shipped as PR #70 (squash 298c30c): the client keeps no store of its own.\n\n**DIAGNOSED 2026-08-10**, and it is olai's, one layer above kolu's merge exactly as suspected — but a CONTRACT violation rather than a keying accident.\n- App.tsx reconciled the day's groups (key `file`) and the outline's rows (key `key`) into stores of its own, and what it handed `reconcile` was BORROWED: `situate`/`rowsFor` mint fresh wrappers, but the records inside them are the served set's own Located objects (derive.ts, dates.ts), and `reconcile` unwraps proxies and mutates the previous objects transitively\n- Read two days in turn and the entries inside a group merge POSITIONALLY (a Situated carries no `file`), while the `shows` records either side of that merge do carry one and it matches — so instead of swapping a reference, reconcile copied one node's id/title/date/desc over another node's record, in the live store, which is the set every other page is read from\n- Those writes then invalidated the very memo they came from (`derived` reads every node), so the effect re-triggered itself until the stack ran out: `RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded`, frames alternating runUpdates ⇄ completeUpdates\n- Observed in the browser on opening a second day; the Dropbox-port sighting above (a node drawn twice, a day missing from the calendar) is the same class\n- Reproduced headlessly against docs/roadmap.jsonl before any fix — the first navigation never converges\n\n**THE FIX:** no store above the framework's.\n- The rows are a memo, a day's groups are read straight off the page model, and identity across frames — the only thing the stores were for — is a KEYING question, answered where the rows are drawn by `<Key>` (@solid-primitives/keyed) on `Row.key` and on `file/id` for a day entry\n- Nothing in the client writes to what the wire hands it, which is now the rule architecture.md states\n\n**E2E:**\n- `Two days, read in turn, each still says what it said` fails on the old client (day 06 lists `pack` twice) and passes on the new one\n- `An outline that arrives beside the open one leaves it whole` closes the new-files gap this entry named — it is green on the old client too, so that gap was coverage rather than a second bug","after":["live"],"see":["live-dead","solid-utilization"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"sigint-hang","parent":"bug-server","ord":"a3","title":"Ctrl+C doesn't stop `just run`","done":"2026-08-10T12:12:41-04:00","desc":"Done-marked 2026-08-10 (human-confirmed): the fix and its regression test shipped inside chat's PR #63 (squash 66d64ff) — this stamp carries that merge instant.\n- Observed 2026-08-10 on the chat branch; a second wedged instance (a store-only smoke server from the previous night) suggests it predates chat\n- **Investigation so far:** SIGINT is delivered and caught (runMain's handler runs), the listener fully closes (no listening socket, no child processes, no TCP connections remain), yet the process never exits — wedged inside Effect scope teardown after all I/O is gone; repeated Ctrl+C is ignored because the handler already tripped\n- **ROOT CAUSE (fixed in PR #63, with the orchestrator's earlier chat-introduced attribution corrected):** NOT chat-specific — master hangs identically whenever a browser tab is connected (the chat agent reproduced it with a master build; the orchestrator's clean master test was an idle server with no tab, the wrong discriminator)\n- server.close waits for every connection, and a tab holds two that never end on their own — the surface websocket and the page's keep-alive — so a server with a tab attached never finished its listener finalizer\n- **Fix:** the teardown now terminates websockets and destroys idle keep-alives before close\n- **Regression test** packages/server/src/shutdown.test.ts: real child process, real websocket, SIGINT, assert exit within a bound — fails against the old finalizer\n- Fix must include a regression test: start the real server, SIGINT it, assert exit within a bound","after":["live"],"see":["serve-surface-app"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"frame-cap","parent":"bug-server","ord":"a4","title":"WS frame cap undercuts the framework's #techdebt","done":"2026-08-10T14:09:23-04:00","desc":"FIXED 2026-08-10, shipped as PR #71 (squash 3822a29): the cap is sourced from the framework.\n- `maxPayload: RPC_MAX_FRAME_BYTES` + the ndjson delimiter (the newline rides the wire but is outside what the decoder measures), so the two layers can no longer disagree whatever either of them is re-pinned to\n- **Correction to the audit's account, measured while fixing it:** under bun — what actually runs this server — `maxPayload` was never enforced at all. Bun's built-in `ws` ignores the option and applies its own 16 MiB ceiling, closing 1006 \"Received too big message\" (16777216 delivered, one byte more killed)\n- So the 8 MiB cap was inert in production and the raw-1009 death was a node host's failure mode; the misconfiguration was real, its symptom was not reachable here\n- That is why the regression fence (`packages/server/src/listener.test.ts`) pins the NUMBER — it fails against the old 8 MiB and against any future drift — beside an end-to-end test that a 9 MiB frame is carried and answered\n- Also newly known: while bun's ceiling stands, the framework's handled INBOUND oversize path is unreachable here at all — a frame the decoder would refuse is already past bun's limit, and even one at exactly the cap arrives a delimiter byte over it and dies at 1006 rather than 1009\n- **Stale:** superseded 2026-08-10 by PR #78, which moved the cap inside serveSurfaceApp as an unspellable framework constant — see serve-surface-app\n\n**Found by the surface-utilization audit (2026-08-09):** listener.ts sets ws maxPayload to 8 MiB while @kolu/surface's frameLimit classifies oversize at 16 MiB — an 8–16 MiB frame (a big outline snapshot) dies at the raw ws layer with close 1009, taking the whole socket down, instead of the framework's handled oversize path.\n- **Fix:** source the cap from the framework's constant, with a test\n- Audit: docs/brainstorming/surface-utilization.md","after":["live"],"see":["serve-surface-app"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"mcp-fail-visible","parent":"bug-mcp","ord":"a0","title":"A failed MCP server is invisible in the UI","done":"2026-08-13T13:51:08-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11, from the kolu-not-detected incident. An MCP server that fails to attach to a chat session must be VISIBLE.\n- **The human's position:** MCP must NOT fail silently\n- **Shipped as PR #140** (squash 1c56f90), 2026-08-13\n  - A strip under the chat panel header — master's three-surface vocabulary, one alarm dot, nothing on a healthy session — states the fact in the server's own words: refused the identity read / closed without answering / did not answer within 5s / could not be started\n  - One probe answers both halves (serverOf / missingFrom); a `servers` event lands on the existing chat cell before every session opens; `MissingServer.where` names the probed binary\n  - \"Never installed\" (no kolu on PATH, no PADI_SOCKET) is deliberately not a failure — but PADI_SOCKET set with kolu absent from the process's PATH is, with its own sentence (the review's crux residual, closed in the delta)\n- **The `/simplify` pass found and fixed a live crash one file over:** a bad OLAI_ACP_AGENT dumped an uncaught ENOENT stack, then blamed `initialize`; the exec-failure axis moved to pipes.ts and both subprocess callers race `unstartable`\n- **Pipeline:** Grok review — zero MUST-FIX; all six NICE-TO-HAVEs taken in the delta (the deadline pin cost 150ms not 5s; the @phone scenario asserts the strip; the NTH#1 test caught the suite reading this machine's ambient PADI_SOCKET)\n- DELTA-OK; CI 10/10 green on kolu-ci-1 at 16b8be5\n- The ci-2/ci-4 ~4m42s e2e walls struck again on two SHAs and were judged host-side by the reviewer — failed logs preserved this time","see":["kolu-detect-primary"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"load-perf","parent":"bug-server","ord":"a5","title":"Roadmap initial load feels very slow","done":"2026-08-12T08:24:51-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 by the human. Symptom: initial load of the roadmap in the web UI is subjectively very slow.\n- Dispatched as measurement + root-cause analysis FIRST — phase breakdown (server load/validate/derive, wire payload, client bundle/render) with hard numbers and a named dominant term; the fix is a separate dispatch after the human reads the RCA\n\n**P0 shipped 2026-08-11:** PR #93 (squash f079b7b).\n- build-time .br/.gz siblings for /assets/*, negotiated by @kolu/surface-app's existing static layer\n- 977 KB → ~253 KB brotli on the wire, browser-verified\n- The RCA and measurement harness were dropped from the PR by the human's own hand (they live in the PR history at 624ffba if ever wanted)\n- P2 shipped separately as snapshot-scale (PR #95)\n- **OPEN:** P1 — code-split markdown/highlight off the critical path (the remaining long-task cost) — undecided, awaiting the human","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"snapshot-scale","parent":"bug-server","ord":"a6","title":"First snapshot carries every document body — must scale to 1000s of .md files","done":"2026-08-11T11:50:45-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11, escalated by the human from load-perf P2: the manifest cell in the FIRST websocket snapshot inlines the full text of every .md document in the served set (~124 KB of the ~212 KB snapshot for docs/, measured in LOAD-PERF-RCA.md).\n- **The human's requirement, verbatim intent:** olai must support directories with THOUSANDS of .md files — a wire that ships every body up front is O(corpus) on first paint and therefore not acceptable, regardless of perf feel today\n\n**Shape:** documents become a collection on the surface — the first snapshot carries only what the sidebar draws (path, title); a body travels when a document is opened (lazy fetch or per-document subscription).\n- This is a WIRE change only: the server still loads and validates the whole set (format.md's rule — doc references must be checkable — is untouched)\n\n**Interactions:**\n- dovetails with surface-mcp-viewing — kolu surface-mcp projects collections as templated resources, so the documents-as-collection shape serves browser and agents alike; the viewing-slice design (terminal d5df9f63, in flight at filing) must anticipate this shape rather than exposing today's body-carrying manifest cell\n- At 1000s of files the server-side whole-set revalidation cost also deserves its own measurement before it surprises anyone — noted here, not scoped here","see":["load-perf","surface-mcp-viewing"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"mirror-status","parent":"bug-tasks","ord":"a0","title":"A mirror does not reflect its target's mark","done":"2026-08-11T13:01:24-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 by the human, seen on the live roadmap.\n- **Bug seen:** a mirror of a node whose target carries doing draws a plain bullet (no checkbox), where the target itself draws the half-filled box\n- Screenshot-confirmed on the \"Markdown rendering, perfected\" pair\n- **Pointer for the fix:** packages/format/src/derive.ts's `Derived.status` doc comment PROMISES mirror coverage (\"a mirror standing for whatever its target stores, since that is what it shows\")\n  - Either the #90 rewrite (stored-only status) dropped the mirror-follows-target hop from the map builder while keeping the comment\n  - Or the row/checkbox path looks the status up under the mirror's own id instead of what it shows\n  - Same question for the blocked index and progressOf: a mirror must ask everything of its TARGET\n- Fix per HACKING.md ships with a test that reproduces: mirror of a doing node shows doing; of a todo node shows todo incl. the empty box; of a done node hides under done-hidden with its subtree ONLY per the done rules; bullet target still shows nothing\n\n**Diagnosed 2026-08-11** (terminal `a1f792c9`, PR #96):\n- NOT a mirror bug — mirrors reflect their target's mark correctly\n- PR #96 (+90/−0, tests+docs) locks that promise at both layers so it cannot silently break: every mark through the rows, both halves of the blocked glyph on a mirror row, done-hidden on a mirror-of-done, and the format.md paragraph (a mirror asks everything of what it shows; a see inherits none of it)\n\n**The screenshot's real cause:**\n- Now entries are regular nodes carrying see (the Now convention dropped real mirrors 2026-08-10 at 849eb9b, because a mirror's four fields cannot hold the terminal/stage/PR prose)\n- A markless node draws a bullet — correct under stored-only status\n- **OPEN, a roadmap-convention call for the human:** should Now entries reflect their item's mark?\n  - (a) back to real mirrors — marks reflect for free, but the prose must live elsewhere\n  - (b) keep see-nodes, status stays a hashtag in the title (today)\n  - (c) mark the Now entries by hand — legal under stored-only, but a second copy to keep in sync\n\n**Shipped 2026-08-11 as PR #96** (squash d4c7df2): the test-lock at both layers plus the format.md paragraph.\n- The Now convention itself was fixed the same day: Now entries are real mirrors again, with the tracking prose on the items\n","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"git-invisible","parent":"bug-git","ord":"a0","title":"Git state is invisible in the UI #human","done":"2026-08-11T19:31:05-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #108** (squash 70f21dd; done carries the merge instant). Final head f3d0a53:\n- Review approve zero must-fixes, three nits taken\n- Applied.why + the Ops.git cell + the header readout (quiet/no-repo/error-with-reason)\n- Reconciled past #106\n- 20 odu nodes green both platforms\n\nFiled 2026-08-11 by the human, hit live on his vault instance.\n- **Bug:** writes through the agent reported `committed: false` with NOTHING in the UI saying so, on a directory he knows is a git repo\n- By design (ops/src/git.ts) the auto-commit cannot fail the write and collapses every cause — no work tree, git missing from the service PATH, staging/commit refusal, identity unset — into the same quiet flag, with the reason only in the server log\n- **The human's ruling, verbatim intent:** \"even if git detection fails I'd expect it to surface in UI — even just 'Not a Git repo' or 'Git error'.\" Errors may still be IGNORED (never block or fail the write); they must be VISIBLE\n- **Shape:** the server knows workTree and each write's committed + git's said — surface a git status affordance in the app chrome (header, near the live dot) showing repo/no-repo/git-error, and let a write's committed: false say why where the reader can see it\n\n**Dispatched 2026-08-11** -> Kolu terminal `b0ff13b8` (Claude Opus, YOLO; worktree .worktrees/git-invisible; brief at .worktrees/git-invisible-BRIEF.md).\n- #stage review — PR #108 (https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/108) open: the boolean becomes values\n  - Applied.why (one sentence on any uncommitted write's reply, additive)\n  - An Ops.git cell (off/repo/none/error + git's words, probed once per serve, republished on refusal and recovery), drawn as a header readout beside the connection pill (quiet healthy, calm no-repo, error with tip)\n- Classification honesty: nothing-to-commit is never a fault; broken-git is error unless git itself said not-a-repository (LC_ALL=C)\n- Non-blocking guarantee kept\n- 572 unit + 185 e2e green locally; three-state evidence in .worktrees/git-invisible-out/\n\n**REVIEW DONE** (Grok, split 0c913c2d, 2026-08-11): APPROVE, zero must-fixes.\n- Non-blocking guarantee holds, three UI states reproduced independently, classification honest, purity clean\n- Three nits: dead code field, isolate onGit from write failure, e2e for Applied.why\n- #stage finishing: nits + master merge past #106 + odu CI; then FIELDED to the human — he decides the merge\n- Reviewer: Grok (cross-model)\n- **Also now a HACKING.md rule** (f2bbd28, the human's own edit): errors are never silently ignored — they surface in the UX\n","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"silent-errors","parent":"bug-server","ord":"a8","title":"Silently ignored errors, inventoried and surfaced #human","done":"2026-08-11T22:34:22-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #112** (squash c5774a7), AUTO-MERGED by the orchestrator 2026-08-12T02:34:04Z under the human's pre-approval (evidence waived by his word; gate: review findings addressed + 18/18 checks at the true head 77c73b6 + roadmap zero-diff).\n- The third autonomous merge of the night\n- The agent held the gate honest itself: it caught that #117's landing staled its earlier green verdict, re-merged, and told the orchestrator NOT to act on the stale green\n\n**The whole swallow inventory surfaced:**\n- Cancels refuse honestly (5-second grace tightened per review)\n- Stream health renders beside the connection pill\n- Store platform failures are DATA with the Banner reading the REASON\n- Kolu failure reasons carried for mcp-fail-visible\n- Unresolvable images name themselves\n- Clipboard denial visible\n- Refused session lists say so\n- Non-text agent chunks render markers\n- `publish?.` is a throw\n- Preferences warn once\n- **Review:** all 12 dimensions passed; findings were hygiene + the cancel-grace question, all addressed\n- /simplify caught two real leaks en route (absolute-path exposure; 60s identical-frame rebroadcast — both regression-tested)\n\n**Filed & Dispatched 2026-08-11** on the human's ask (a paste that did nothing; the audit that followed found the three reverted PRs — see docs/RCA/) -> Kolu terminal `c65479b2` (Claude Opus, YOLO; reviewer Grok, split `b9daf69c`).\n- Part 1 (paste restore) split out and shipped as #111\n","see":["git-invisible","mcp-fail-visible","chat"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"paste-restore","parent":"bug-chat","ord":"a8","title":"Restore paste-image: revert the mis-titled dd34849","done":"2026-08-11","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #111** (squash 2de0ef5), merged BY THE HUMAN directly at 2026-08-11T19:42:50-04:00 (this done stamp is the ops-layer instant, ~minutes after; review and refactor waived by the human).\n- Grok cherry-picked dc4c078, verified the restored e2e coverage, odu green both platforms\n\n**Filed & Dispatched 2026-08-11** (split from silent-errors at the human's direction: separate quick PR) -> Kolu terminal `b3e45fe0` (Grok, always-approve; worktree .worktrees/paste-restore).\n- Cherry-picks dc4c078 (the completed revert-of-dd34849, authored by the silent-errors Opus)\n- Verifies the RESTORED e2e coverage passes (the tests dd34849 deleted are the regression fence that was missing)\n- odu CI both platforms, PR against master\n- **Process, set by the human:** NO review, NO refactor pass — quick; orchestrator fields the PR at green\n","see":["paste-image","silent-errors"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"restore-84","parent":"bug-outline","ord":"a0","title":"Restore title-markdown: revert the mis-titled a56cb65","done":"2026-08-11T20:28:17-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #113** (squash ae59f9e), merged BY THE HUMAN directly at 2026-08-12T00:27:53Z (this done stamp is the ops instant just after; review and refactor waived per the quick-restore process).\n- Inline markdown in titles is back on master, reconciled to coexist with #102's tag pills in one title\n- #84's restored tests pass beside #102's\n\n**Filed & Dispatched 2026-08-11** -> Kolu terminal `c7118f67` (Grok, always-approve).\n- **Origin:** the orchestrator's stamp-commit audit found a56cb65 ('roadmap: title-markdown done (#84)', seconds after the #84 merge) to be the exact content-inverse of squash e1ab412 outside docs/roadmap.jsonl\n- The third mass-revert stamp from the same morning session (with dd34849/#87 and 12ea294/#83)\n- Inline title markdown had been absent from master ever since, while the ledger read done\n","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"sticky-header","parent":"bug-nav","ord":"a0","title":"Header scrolls away — must be sticky","done":"2026-08-11T21:35:40-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #115** (squash df67730), AUTO-MERGED by the orchestrator 2026-08-12T01:35:17Z under the human's conditional pre-approval.\n- The visual gate passed on inspection (desktop scrolled deep with the header pinned; phone drawer from a scrolled page still meeting the header seam)\n- Review: approve, zero must-fixes (Grok drove both viewports, spot-checked the diagnostic e2e by reverting the fix)\n- 18/18 required checks green at f83a527; one darwin FSEvents flake in an untouched package flagged honestly, rerun, passed\n- 7 diagnostic e2e each proven failing on the pre-change client\n- **Deliberately untouched:** the desktop sidebar still scrolls with the page — filed as sidebar-sticky for the human's ratification\n\n**Filed & Dispatched 2026-08-11** by the human (screen recording; it showed the page at rest, so the author reproduced the scroll-away itself — header at y=-4963 — before fixing) -> Kolu terminal `b2b467d6` (Claude Opus, YOLO).\n- Interacting chrome kept true: #104's drawer/scrim/sheet anchor at `top-[var(--height-header)]`, contents jumps land clear of the bar (scroll-padding)\n","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"commit-whole-repo","parent":"bug-git","ord":"a1","title":"Commit UI is blind to edits outside the ops path — .md edits don't show as pending","done":"2026-08-12T13:26:42-04:00","desc":"**Shipped in PR #122** (squash 518f4af, merged 2026-08-12T17:25:56Z, human-approved and human-merged). Everything the human ratified at dispatch landed:\n\n**PHASE ONE:**\n- git.ts extracted to leaf package @olai/git (one dep: effect)\n- Audit convention as an argument, trailer returned verbatim for ops to classify\n- RepoState/Reason owned by the git package, format re-exporting on a `./state` subpath so the browser never reaches `node:child_process`\n- Every plumbing subtlety preserved\n\n**THE FEATURE:**\n- Pending grew outlines/others/served/unpushed\n- The survey lifted to the repository root (a dirty root README.md shows while serving docs/)\n- Dirty non-outline files are path-level rows with porcelain-derived kind chips, untracked included, .gitignore respected\n- PIECEMEAL commits are a selection of named paths, never the index — hand-staged work untouched, refused-by-name for paths with nothing waiting\n- PUSH arrived on both faces (Ops.push, MCP push tool, panel button, header pill count via one survey), refusals verbatim, Blocked-naming-the-rebase like commit\n- `--commit=auto` unchanged\n\n**Review** (Grok, two passes) caught two real MUST-FIXes:\n- A REFUSED commit leaked the git add into the real index (fixed — index bit-identical after failure, test proven against the reviewer's own gpgsign repro)\n- The stale git README\n- `--no-gpg-sign` deliberately refused (a signature is the owner's statement; gpg's refusal carries verbatim)\n\n**Also fixed from review:**\n- pill/panel fence unified (a reformatted outline with zero node changes counts as waiting)\n- git-status failure surfaces as the Unusable/git-error face\n- docs folded into #123's docs/git.md\n- Side find filed separately: mcp-stdout-pollution\n\n- 914 unit + 261 e2e at review; CI green both platforms\n- **FOLLOW-UP for the orchestrator:** reconnect the olai MCP server to gain the push tool and the paths-arg commit — then the orchestrator's last raw-git verb (git push) retires\n","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"one-git-indicator","parent":"bug-git","ord":"a2","title":"Two git indicators in the header — there should be one","done":"2026-08-11T22:54:54-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #119** (squash b1ca909), AUTO-MERGED by the orchestrator 2026-08-12T02:54:36Z under the overnight pre-approval — fourth autonomous merge.\n- **Gate record:** the review's DO-NOT-MERGE round did its job (the 390pt shrink order had traded one wrap bug for another — the CONNECTION pill went illegible)\n- The fix round resolved it and the orchestrator's visual gate confirmed on the refreshed 40-image evidence: \"● live\" fully legible at 390pt both themes, the commit pill the graceful truncator (glyph intact), exactly one git indicator in every shot, verified in the pinned bar\n- 22 odu checks green at e045c73 both platforms; roadmap zero-diff; conflicts with #112 resolved keeping both sides\n- The one-indicator claim is now a control-shaped e2e assertion\n\nFiled 2026-08-11 by the human (screenshot: \"● git\" beside \"✓ committed · 3m ago\").\n- **Dispatched** (overnight slate) -> Kolu terminal `7184295a` (Claude Opus, YOLO; reviewer Grok, split `a18ec355`)\n- Bonus: fixed a pre-existing 390pt wordmark-crush bug found while shooting evidence\n","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"load-perf-p1","parent":"load-perf","ord":"a0","title":"P1: markdown/highlight off the critical path","done":"2026-08-12T08:24:20-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #118** (squash 59e4192), AUTO-MERGED by the orchestrator 2026-08-12T12:23:45Z under the overnight pre-approval — fifth and final autonomous merge of the slate.\n- **Gate record:** review zero must-fixes with the reviewer running its OWN adversarial network/remount script (outline pages fetch no markdown chunk; markdown-bearing pages fetch once; no remount on a held document)\n- Numbers verified honest and reproducible: document words-on-screen −30.8% (203.7→140.9ms), fully-rendered +0–35ms disclosed as run-variance, main chunk byte-for-byte reproducible at the head\n- 18/18 checks both platforms at f44297e; roadmap zero-diff\n- The upstream ask lives as splitting-upstream (filed by the orchestrator)\n\n**Dispatched 2026-08-11** (overnight slate) -> Kolu terminal `4a78220a` (Claude Opus, YOLO; reviewer Grok, split `43698764`)\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"sidebar-sticky","parent":"bug-nav","ord":"a1","title":"Desktop sidebar scrolls away with the page — should it pin like the header?","done":"2026-08-12T11:21:36-04:00","desc":"**Shipped in PR #121** (squash 37648ee, merged 2026-08-12T15:20:50Z) — the human's first same-day pre-approved auto-merge.\n- **Full pipeline:** Grok adversarial review: NO must-fix; odu CI 20/20 both platforms at 219d4ae\n- Then the orchestrator's visual gate on the evidence: before — empty column at deep scroll; after — calendar+tree pinned under the header, collapsed rail pinned, column's own scroll independent of the page, phone shots sha256-identical before/after\n- **What shipped:** desktop sidebar (calendar + file tree + icon rail) pins below the #115 header with its own scroll region\n- #105 collapsed-by-default and ⌘\\ survive; mobile drawer untouched; #102 styling not regressed\n- **One non-CSS change:** scroll.ts gained a bounded frame-by-frame clamp-restore retry (1s / takeover / position-holds) because the page-tall column had been quietly propping up document height — regression fence proven failing without it (zoom_and_navigate 1px short)\n- Review corrected a false PR-body claim (3 'pre-existing' bun failures — actually 878/0 green both sides)\n- **Known residuals, recorded as decisions in the PR:** SETTLE_MS=1000 doesn't close the slow-/media/* restore case (predates the pin); the collapse chevron overlays a scrolled tree's foot (#105's control, newly visible)\n","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"precompress-dev-tax","parent":"bug-build","ord":"a0","title":"Precompression taxes every dev-server start ~20s — recompresses a never-pruned dist","done":"2026-08-12T21:28:58-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-12 from the human hitting it live (\"this compress stuff is slowing down the dev server like 20 seconds\").\n- **CLOSED 2026-08-13** by PR #129's pin bump — the taxed file no longer exists, and the filed symptom is unreachable\n- Measured on the merged path (buildSurfaceClient → pruneAssets → precompressAssets): cold 3.87s · no-op rebuild 0.96s · changed-entry rebuild 2.18s\n- dist/assets stable at 19 files over four consecutive builds\n\n- **Leg (a) prune — paid upstream** (kolu#2159 names this downstream case in its own body): the hashed dir is reduced to what this build produced before anything is compressed.\n- **Leg (b) skip — paid upstream**: an identically-hashed sibling is left alone; the skip keys on emitted bytes, not source mtime (a minified-away comment does not re-pay).\n- **Leg (c) dev-skip flag — overtaken by ruling**: kolu#2159 refused the precompress knob BY NAME (\"the switch would only ever select between 'the layer works' and 'the layer has nothing to serve'\"). Not implementable in olai; re-opening it is a NEW upstream ask against that ruling, not this node.\n- **Residual, intended**: a build whose emitted bytes changed pays ~1.2s compressing the changed files (slightly up per-file — .zst is a third encoding now — while the total collapsed). Bounded, not growing.\n","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"editor-op-parity","parent":"bug-edit","ord":"a0","title":"Web editor expresses less than MCP — a standing HACKING consistency violation","done":"2026-08-14T12:33:42-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-12 from the human's Editor-subtree review.\n- HACKING.md says \"MCP and Web ops must be consistent; never deviate\" — they deviated, so this was a BUG\n\n**PIPELINE COMPLETE 2026-08-14**, PR #166 AWAITS THE HUMAN'S APPROVAL (lane `b9cc35e3` alive; reviewer splits idle).\n- see-edges and after-edges writable from the web (widget-family creation via the `((` machinery, × removal, acyclicity refusals verbatim and sabotage-pinned)\n- The sidebar mints outlines (op's validation verbatim) — all through the intent seam, three arms on the union, three in the resolver, no side channels\n- **Panel review** (grok 0+2, opencode 0+2, independently CONVERGENT on the same two nits; both confirm the deviation closed): union addressed at 9cbb779\n  - The one-verb prose is three verbs in four places\n  - Feature pins added for both new exclusions\n  - SeeRefs.tsx reference corrected\n  - Edge-undo e2e'd for after and × removal (the append-order residual asserted as documented behavior)\n  - The edge-search step keys its wait on the query\n- Five sabotages on the evidence page, each red on its claimed pin\n- CI 9/9 required at 9cbb779, MERGEABLE/CLEAN; 539 e2e scenarios, 1519 unit tests\n- Evidence: https://claude.ai/code/artifact/2581c0b9-099a-4b44-bb6a-060669ec9d70\n\n- **Children closed by this PR at merge:** parity-see, parity-after, parity-create-outline (stamps land with the merge)\n- **Deferred, named on the PR:** the append-order residual itself (a set_see change, not an undo change), per-row createEdgeEditing signals, edgesOf's algorithmic coupling to the planner\n","see":["undo","input-widgets","silent-errors"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"parity-archive","parent":"editor-op-parity","ord":"a0","title":"archive: MCP archive_node vs no web affordance at all","done":"2026-08-18T02:55:00-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED for the mouse in PR #124** (`menu-verbs`, squash 60631fe, 2026-08-12); this stamp is the bookkeeping that never landed.\n- The human's ruling that day was SUBTREE WITH A CONFIRM, and that is what the `•••` menu's `Move to Trash` sends\n- One `archive` edit through the same gate `archive_node` goes through, behind a question naming how many rows go\n- Counted over the SET rather than over the rows on screen (done-hiding drops finished branches from a reading, and a count that read the page would understate what the write moves)\n- **NO KEY, deliberately:** there is still no delete key in this app, and the roadmap's own \"key only if the human wants one\" was never answered yes\n- Three doors reach the op now, all asking the same catalog (`web/src/client/menu/verbs.ts`): the row's `•••`, the multi-selection bar, and the ⌘K palette on a zoomed node — the one node no pointer could put away, since a heading has no `•••`\n- A MIRROR ROW IS NOT OFFERED IT (see `parity-remove-mirror`)\n- What the write did is on the Trash: `parity-unarchive` gave the archive its way out, and #226 took what is put away off every other page\n- Pinned by `menu_verbs.feature` (offers, asks, the count, cancel, confirm) and `trash.feature`; the verbs and the confirm are unit-tested beside them\n- **Stamped 2026-08-18** by the `web-archive-unmirror` lane, dispatched on this node's own stale desc — it still read \"the web has NO archive verb, key, or menu entry\", false since 2026-08-12\n  - Committed the evidence sections `move-to-trash-from-the-menu` and `retire-a-placement` (`packages/tests/evidence.ts`) so the pair is photographed rather than only asserted\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"parity-date","parent":"editor-op-parity","ord":"a1","title":"date: MCP set_date (set AND clear) vs no web date editing","done":"2026-08-13T00:38:39-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #133 (95c3a8b), squash-merged 2026-08-13. The web sets and changes a date on the row — the picker, reachable from the date badge and the ••• menu (Set date… / Change date…), sending the same `date` edit #124's Clear already put on the wire.\n\n- **Dates stay text**: `input type=\"date\"` chosen because it cannot mint an instant — the ten picked characters are the ten written; the only reading is @olai/format's dayOf. Sabotage via toISOString went red.\n- **One spelling of clear**: the picker absorbs #124's verb — emptying the box flips the button to Clear date and both doors emit ONE constructor's edit, with a two-door divergence test (review MUST-FIX; sabotage-verified so the split cannot silently return).\n- **The agenda is the consumer, proven**: a past date on a todo moves it into Overdue live, no reload — pinned in e2e (isOverdue sabotage turned 9 cases red).\n- **Evidence caught two bugs pre-review** (empty said-box under the menu; Clear date offered undated) — both fixed and pinned; the author also caught its OWN first e2e pin passing under sabotage (absence-wait always succeeds) and rewrote it read-once.\n- **Recorded, not lost**: touch door for undated rows (the ••• menu is pointer-only below md — the checkbox's same gap) and three /simplify skips, in the PR body.\n- **CI**: 10/10 Linux at c186fca; the sick-pool file is now three-for-three (mid-suite kill ~4½min, truncated log, committing.feature untouched by the PR — kolu-ci-2 and ci-3 implicated, ci-1 green throughout; table in the PR comment).\n- **Evidence** (verified by the orchestrator): picker from badge, picker from menu, the before/after Overdue move, the absorbed clear — archived to the session scratchpad."}
{"id":"parity-marks","parent":"editor-op-parity","ord":"a2","title":"todo/doing marks: MCP set_todo + set_doing vs web toggles done only","done":"2026-08-12T22:52:22-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #132 (f5d130d), squash-merged 2026-08-13. The web writes all three marks without inventing a second writer: ⌘⇧Enter is an INTENT (`walk`) — the server reads the stored mark and emits exactly the ops request an agent would send.\n\n- **The ring**: unmarked → todo → doing → unmarked; unmarked is a stop (the field leaves the record), `done` is deliberately OFF the ring (walking through it would stamp an instant, fire the nudge, and hide the row en route to somewhere else — Ctrl+Enter stays done's own verb).\n- **The refusal is met, not absorbed**: on a finished row the walk asks todo outright and ops' verbatim sentence renders under the row, naming the way through (undo first — two ops, the second the person's).\n- **Bug found and fixed on the way**: `inverseOf` applied two-edit undo whenever a mark displaced another; the rule is only for writes that leave a node done — undo of the menu's Clear-mark was already broken by this. Regression pinned.\n- **Review**: NO MUST-FIX, six hunts held, three sabotages red on their claimed pins. NTHs: mirror-disk tautology assertion dropped + ring-inverse coverage widened; the data-tone markup-for-a-test declined (the sentence is the contract via its testid). Menu verbs and Archive pre-exist from #124 — this PR is keyboard + refusal + inverse only.\n- **CI**: 10/10 Linux at the resolved head; the sick-host file grew hard data (base commit fails identically on kolu-ci-3/4 with none of this PR's changes; green on a free pool).\n- **Evidence** (verified by the orchestrator): all four faces in one glance, the walk stepwise, the refusal verbatim, the two-step through it, menu verbs, keys written down in docs/editing.md — archived to the session scratchpad."}
{"id":"parity-see","parent":"editor-op-parity","ord":"a3","title":"see edges: MCP set_see add/remove vs web renders but cannot write","done":"2026-08-14T12:33:37-04:00","desc":"MCP adds and removes see references; the web RENDERS them (edges-ui, done) but has no affordance to create or remove one. Creation wants a node search (the same widget family as input-widgets' `((` mirror search); removal wants an x on the rendered reference or a ••• verb."}
{"id":"parity-after","parent":"editor-op-parity","ord":"a4","title":"after edges: MCP set_after vs web shows blocked state but cannot change it","done":"2026-08-14T12:33:38-04:00","desc":"MCP adds and removes after dependencies (#117 completed the set); the web draws blockedness (edges-ui) but a person cannot declare or lift a dependency. Same widget family as parity-see; acyclicity refusals must surface verbatim per HACKING."}
{"id":"parity-remove-mirror","parent":"editor-op-parity","ord":"a5","title":"mirror removal: MCP remove_mirror vs no web way to retire a placement","done":"2026-08-18T02:55:00-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED for the mouse in PR #124** (`menu-verbs`, squash 60631fe, 2026-08-12); this stamp is the bookkeeping that never landed.\n- The `•••` menu on a MIRROR row offers `Remove this placement` and does not offer `Move to Trash` — the split this verb exists for\n- What the reader is looking at is a line standing for a node that lives somewhere else, and archiving from there would file a subtree out of sight on a click that reads as being about this line\n- The question is asked of the row's OWN RECORD rather than of what it managed to draw (`web/src/client/menu/verbs.ts`), so the two degenerate placements — a chain that died, one that closed a loop — are covered by construction rather than by a fence\n- **THE OP'S FENCE REACHES THE CLICK VERBATIM:** a placement something else still names is refused naming what to re-point first, exactly as `remove_mirror` refuses it\n- Pinned by `menu_verbs.feature` (\"Retiring a placement takes the line and leaves the node\", \"A placement something else still names is refused, naming what\")\n- The creation half is `input-widgets`' `((`, whose ⌘Z is an `unmirror`\n- The retire itself is the one write on this surface with no inverse, said by recording nothing rather than by a ⌘Z that would mint a different id in a slot it cannot name (`server/src/edit.ts`)\n- **Stamped 2026-08-18** by the `web-archive-unmirror` lane, dispatched on this node's own stale desc — \"the web has no affordance on a mirror row\", false since 2026-08-12\n  - Also documented the verb in docs/editing.md (it was the one menu WRITE that doc never named)\n  - Committed the `retire-a-placement` evidence section\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"parity-create-outline","parent":"editor-op-parity","ord":"a6","title":"create outline: MCP create_outline vs no web new-file affordance","done":"2026-08-14T12:33:38-04:00","desc":"MCP mints a new .jsonl outline (optionally seeded with a tree); the web sidebar lists files but cannot create one. A \"new outline\" affordance in the sidebar; naming/path validation is the op's, surfaced verbatim."}
{"id":"parity-unarchive","parent":"editor-op-parity","ord":"a7","title":"unarchive: missing on BOTH faces — the trash cannot be taken out of","done":"2026-08-13T19:05:02-04:00","desc":"The equal absence the 2026-08-12 review exposed: UNARCHIVE existed on NO face. **Shipped as PR #147 (squash 7457d9ab), 2026-08-13**, under the human's shape ruling.\n- The archive got a real web view named **Trash** (file and MCP vocabulary unchanged): sidebar entry, read-only rows, \"Put back\" per row\n- The ops verb born once, exposed on both faces\n- ⌘⇧Z genuinely brings a row back out (pinned, including a retitled-parent scenario added when the review's own suggestion stayed green under sabotage)\n- **The review's MUST-FIX** (Put back on a minted ancestor husk minted live duplicates — proven by planner runs) fixed red-first at the ops layer: the notASignpost fence (bare + a live twin at the landing) refuses on both faces identically\n- Put back deliberately NOT hidden client-side, to avoid recreating the faces split\n- Archive/remove-mirror menu verbs were #124's (verified, not rebuilt; archive relabeled \"Move to Trash\")\n- **Escalated to the human, still open:** does the set freeze archived work, or stay editable on both faces (today: editable, symmetric — recorded in editing-web.md's Open)\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"chat-restore-wrong","parent":"bug-chat","ord":"a0","title":"Restart restores the wrong chat: newest-in-directory is an identity guess","done":"2026-08-13T23:12:05-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-14 on the human's report: after olai restarts, the panel restored some OTHER session.\n- Boot adopted the newest-by-updatedAt session in the served directory, an identity guess anything fresher could steal.\n- **MERGED 2026-08-13** (night slate, SIMPLE — autonomous merge per the human's overnight authorization): PR #156, squashed at master.\n  - The panel's session id is now olai's own note (chat `memory.ts`, under `$XDG_STATE_HOME`): written when the panel enters a conversation, read back at boot.\n  - Newest-in-directory demoted to first-boot/gone fallback.\n  - Picker rows carry honest local timestamps.\n  - CodeQL's polynomial-redos finding on the trailing-slash regex fixed by counting slashes.\n- **Evidence:** e2e scenario fails on the old `stored[0]` behavior, 50/50 scenarios pass with the fix.\n- **Grok review:** 1 blocking + 2 nits (all doc staleness), addressed at 935d5705; 9/9 required Linux checks green.\n- The superseded-by-hint dead end moved to its own node under Bugs (#upstream #human).","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"superseded-hint-upstream","parent":"bug-chat","ord":"a1","title":"Session list can't show \"superseded by\" — the adapter gives no data #upstream #human","todo":true,"desc":"- The adapter's listSessions returns only {sessionId, cwd, title, updatedAt}, and ACP has no message count — so the planned superseded hint and per-row counts have nothing to read.\n- Any fix is upstream (adapter `_meta`, or ACP SessionInfo). Needs the human's go-ahead before filing on another repo.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:02:58-04:00"}
{"id":"undo-feature-flaky","parent":"bug-tests","ord":"a0","title":"undo.feature races a write against the assertion after it #techdebt","done":"2026-08-14T09:00:48-04:00","desc":"The e2e flake was one mistake in six places: a write goes out through a DRAFT, the draft is the only receipt this tab gives, and no key step waited for it.\n- **MERGED 2026-08-14** (PR #164, the human approved, squashed at 96b1dfb).\n  - \"I press\" / \"I type\" / \"I select all and type\" / \"I click away\" now wait for the caret to be in the line before aiming, and to leave the PLACE (`Row.key`: chain + seat) after — or for the page to say why not.\n  - \"I press … without waiting\" remains for the two scenarios that mean the race.\n  - Two disk assertions fixed: waiting readers go through `world.servedNodesSoFar` (ENOENT and nothing else — a non-JSON line still faults).\n  - The holding-negative \"holds no node titled\" split from its waiting twin (five holding uses remain, listed on the PR).\n- **Proof:** 5/5 undo runs and 3/3 five-feature runs failed under load before; 12/12 green after, 12/12 again post-`/simplify`, 3/3 after the review round.\n  - No timeout raised, no retry added, no claim loosened — red runs now name what they waited for (mutant-proven wording).\n- CI 9/9 required at 96b1dfb.\n- **Two product findings reported, not fixed**, each its own node under Bugs: new-line-blur-caret and client-quiescence (#human).\n- **MERGE-ORDER NOTE for the open PRs:** #159 and #162 each carry their own copies of the two disk fixes.\n  - Whichever lands after this conflicts textually in `editing_steps.ts` — keep THIS reader (`servedNodesSoFar`, ENOENT only) and one copy of the step.\n  - Their local `recordsIn` blanket-catch swallows malformed records and must not survive.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"client-quiescence","parent":"bug-tests","ord":"a1","title":"The client never says when it has finished handling a key #human","todo":true,"desc":"- A refused key redraws nothing, so nobody (tests included) can tell a second refusal from the first; under load this once corrupted a typed title.\n- Receipts now cover keys that move the caret; keys that redraw in place (Ctrl+Enter and the mark walk) still have none.\n- Honest fix: the client publishes its own quiescence — a counter bumped when a key is queued, cleared when the queue drains. Covers every key at once.\n- A product change made for tests: the human's call.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:02:58-04:00"}
{"id":"new-line-blur-caret","parent":"bug-edit","ord":"a1","title":"Clicking away from a brand-new line leaves the caret in the row it just made","done":"2026-08-15T16:47:25-04:00","desc":"FINDING from PR #164's era (2026-08-14): clicking away from a brand-new line left the caret in the row it just made.\n- **MERGED 2026-08-15** (pre-approved on the orchestrator's visual verification): PR #187, squashed at 4d031cb.\n- **Root cause** exactly the node's hypothesis: every caret keeps its address for life EXCEPT a brand-new line's.\n  - The write that lands it mints the row's id, so the blur guard read \"the reader moved\" about a reader who never did.\n- **Fix:** the landed row carries the slot it was typed at (`Editing.was` — one writer, one reader, always-a-row forwards nothing, sabotage-proven); blur asks `stillAt`.\n- Three red-first scenarios across all three anchors.\n  - The disclosed timing window (click inside `IDLE_COMMIT` or the idle timer masks the bug) proven asymmetric by review — a slow runner gets a loud timeout, never a silent pass.\n- **Reviews:** Grok + opencode, zero blocking, zero nits.\n- The orchestrator verified the before/after frames by eye: an open editor where the click should have landed, then nothing being typed.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"input-widgets-escape-flake","parent":"bug-edit","ord":"a2","title":"input_widgets.feature:209 flakes: Escape sometimes fails to close the editor draft #e2e","done":"2026-08-15T17:39:32-04:00","desc":"Caught loose during PR #171's night run (2026-08-14), grok's attribution; bit at least five separate runs across the week.\n- **HUNTED 2026-08-15** (Grok author, terminal `06697db6`): THE FLAKE WAS REAL, AND DOUBLE.\n  1. Escape could resurrect the draft it had just dismissed (isolated repro red on run 3/200, state captured).\n  2. With that fixed alone, a too-early ⌘Z still tripped it at run 150.\n- Both fixed in PR #190.\n- **Proof discipline:** both-fixes 300/300 on :209, neighbors 100/100, full suite clean, unit `kept(null, held)` red-then-green.\n- CI 9/9 at d3e6a75.\n- **Stage:** #review — opencode SOLE reviewer per the human (`91e57e62`), briefed to re-derive both mechanisms from the captured states and loop the proof at its own timing.\n- FIELDED to srid; merge is his word.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"watcher-postboot-blind","parent":"bug-server","ord":"a7","title":"A directory created after boot is invisible to the watcher until the 60s backstop","done":"2026-08-15T21:36:05-04:00","desc":"Found 2026-08-14 by the watcher-fd-cost investigation, in what ships today (bun 1.3.13's watcher, Linux).\n- Create a file in a post-boot subdirectory → NO EVENT; edit it → NO EVENT.\n- Only `store.ts:157`'s 60s poll backstop keeps this from being a correctness bug.\n- Measured shape-by-shape; the method and transcript are in `docs/brainstorming/watcher-fd-cost.md`.\n- Fixed upstream by bun 1.3.14's watcher rewrite (the same bump that drops 1050 fds to 15).\n- This node closes with whichever bump path the human rules on bun-watcher-bump, and exists so the blind spot is not forgotten if that ruling waits.","see":["bun-watcher-bump"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00","custom":{"pr":"196"}}
{"id":"tests-stray-debris","parent":"bug-tests","ord":"a2","title":"Stray probe files committed to packages/tests, one hardcoding a dead worktree path","done":"2026-08-15T17:47:07-04:00","desc":"Found by the sidebar-pierre-tree lane (2026-08-15).\n\n- **Found:** packages/tests/_h.ts and _probe.ts — agents' probe scripts accidentally committed, one hardcoding a dead worktree path.\n- **RESOLVED** the same day by the human's ruling: no CI check, just hygiene.\n  - Both files git-rm'd directly on master (718e312e).\n  - The human's own \"no junk files\" line committed to HACKING.md (aa23635e).\n- The check-that-would-catch-them idea lives on at stray-file-green-ci, unratified.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"chat-model-stale","parent":"bug-chat","ord":"a2","title":"The chat header's model goes stale after /model","done":"2026-08-15T11:16:32-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-15 by the human with a screenshot.\n\n- **Diagnosed** systemic: the picker's values are adapter ALIASES while the live system/init id is CANONICAL.\n- labels.get() missed all five rows, so the stale-model warning fired on every change ever and the header answered raw or stale.\n\n**Now** (2026-08-15):\n- Kolu terminal: `485cd9bb`, branch `chat-model-stale`, PR #176 at head 46db630.\n- **Review round done:**\n  - Grok: 1 BLOCKING — constructed the lie (\"Opus (1M context)\" on a 200k session) — plus nits.\n  - opencode: 2 nits.\n  - **ALL ADDRESSED:**\n    - The lane-borrowing inference is gone: an undated live id resolves, a dated pin shows raw, the opus lie is REFUSED (one scenario drives all three arms; cost paid deliberately: a common alias now shows as a raw id).\n    - The if(running) guard deleted on its own demerits (a refusal fallback re-picks via config_option_update — back to whichever-moved-last-wins, pinned by a reconfig scenario).\n    - Video caption corrected.\n    - docs/chat.md documents the refusal.\n  - **Deferred** (argued on the record): no test for first-live-id-disagrees-at-boot — needs a per-scenario spawn knob for one assertion; no baseline branch left to regress into.\n- **Stage:** CI at 46db630 running under the author's monitor, then FIELDED to the human; PR 2 (chat-token-usage) cuts only after his word on PR 1.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"commit-op-staged-rename","parent":"bug-git","ord":"a3","title":"PR: pending and commit learn the index — a staged rename stops reading as a deletion","done":"2026-08-15T14:30:39-04:00","desc":"One hole, two faces, two live reproductions (2026-08-15): the pending/commit machinery reads the working tree against HEAD and never reads the INDEX, so hand-staged work — renames above all — is invisible or misclassified.\n\n- **MCP face** (orchestrator, fixing the docs/docs mint): with `git mv old new` staged, the commit op failed \"pathspec old did not match any files\" instead of committing the rename or refusing in its own words.\n- **WEB face** (the human's vault, post-.olai migration): `git mv`'d Archive.jsonl→Archive.olai and Tasks.jsonl→Tasks.olai staged.\n  - Commit panel showed \"Archive.jsonl deleted\" / \"Tasks.jsonl deleted\" — renames unread, the new .olai files invisible.\n  - Committing died with `fatal: pathspec '/home/srid/Vault/Archive.jsonl' did not match any files` — git's words surfaced raw because the sweep offered a path that exists only in HEAD.\n- **THE HUMAN'S CONSTRAINT**, binding on whoever takes this: REPRODUCE IN A TEST FIRST — a failing test holding a hand-staged rename against both the pending view and the commit path, before any fix lands.\n  - The fix reads the index (staged state) as part of pending, draws a rename as a rename, and never hands git a HEAD-only path.\n- **Related but separate:** create_outline minted docs/docs silently when handed the served root's own name — a refusal wanting a sentence (kept here so the two path-shaped stumbles travel together).","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"external-links-newtab","parent":"bug-nav","ord":"a2","title":"An external link opens in a new tab","done":"2026-08-15T12:31:56-04:00","desc":"Filed and fixed 2026-08-15 the same afternoon (the ledger was frozen at filing time — this node is the after-the-fact record, the freeze's one debt).\n\n- **Bug:** an external link rendered in olai navigated the app tab away.\n- **MERGED** as PR #180 (squash, review WAIVED by the human, Grok 4.6 solo author — its first authoring lane here).\n  - Cross-origin http/https anchors gain target=_blank rel=noopener noreferrer at render time.\n  - /doc/ links, node navigation and anchors untouched, pinned in render.test.ts's own style.\n  - CI 9/9 required at fbf49eee.\n- **Grok-TUI quirk** recorded for future dispatches: a paste during boot needs a second Enter once the footer says send-now.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"chat-diff-wrap","parent":"bug-chat","ord":"a3","title":"PR: the chat's diffs wrap — no horizontal scrollbar in the panel","done":"2026-08-15T15:32:13-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-15 by the human with a screenshot: an agent's file-edit diff in the ACP chat clipped long lines behind a horizontal scrollbar.\n\n- **MERGED** the same day (pre-approved on verified evidence): PR #185, squashed at 61f22f0.\n  - Content wraps inside the box (grid + the min-w-0 chain on Panel/Entry/ToolFrame/Transcript/DropTarget, overflow-x-hidden on the transcript, both halves credited).\n  - Gutter and +/- keep their column across wrapping add, remove and same rows, pinned with 700-character UNBROKEN tokens of each kind.\n- Grok authored; opencode sole reviewer per the human (nothing blocking, 3 nits fixed); CI 9/9 at head.\n- **Evidence:** the orchestrator verified the before/after by eye on laptop and phone before firing — the before shows the token escaping the box, the after wraps mid-token with the gutter intact.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"suite-load-flakes","parent":"bug-tests","ord":"a3","title":"Under load, the e2e suite drops 1–3 unrelated scenarios — never the same twice #e2e","done":"2026-08-15T23:47:22-04:00","desc":"Named independently by three lanes and two reviewers on 2026-08-15 (props, one-Site, caret, html-preview runs all saw it).\n\n- A full or tag-filtered suite on a box hosting other worktrees' servers intermittently fails 1–3 UNRELATED scenarios: inbox capture, a date pill, server restart, palette, edge editing, ⌘Z pair.\n- 15s timeouts, always green in isolation and on re-run, never twice on the same scenario.\n- Not any PR's diff — parallel workers vs machine load.\n- Distinct from the FIXED Escape flake (#190, a real bug).\n- **Hunt:** starts with worker-count vs load instrumentation; the fix may be as dull as backoff on the 15s step timeout under load — but measured, per the house law.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00","custom":{"pr":"199"}}
{"id":"chat-speaker-discern","parent":"bug-chat","ord":"a4","title":"PR: the human's chat messages are hard to tell from the agent's","done":"2026-08-15T18:38:28-04:00","desc":"Reported by the human 2026-08-15 with a screenshot (kept at /tmp/olai-dispatch/chat-discern-before.png).\n\n- In the web chat panel, the human's own messages (\"scrim?\", \"I confirm Esc does dismiss…\") render nearly identically to the agent's.\n- A faint box is the only cue, and it does not read as a speaker change.\n- **Fix:** visual differentiation of the human's messages in the chat transcript.\n- Dispatched to grok as AUTHOR at the human's explicit instruction, with no reviewer lane — a deliberate exception to agents.olai's reviewer-only contract for grok.\n- The PR must include before/after visual evidence (screenshots), per the human's dispatch order.","created":"2026-08-15T18:00:51-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00","custom":{"agent":"grok","pr":"191"}}
{"id":"client-draw-crash","parent":"bug-outline","ord":"a1","title":"The web page crashes while drawing: \"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'remove')\"","done":"2026-08-16T11:07:05-04:00","desc":"Seen 2026-08-16, mid-chat, on the production build (myolai.rooster-blues.ts.net). The whole page dies to the \"This page broke\" screen.\n\n- **Window:** the human says it started in the last ~24 hours of PRs — #192 through #200.\n  - Of those, #192 hits-carry-custom, #195 search-props-ui and #197 html-frame-height touched client drawing; #200 was tests-only.\n- The throw is inside the UI framework's own list-reconciliation code, not olai's (frames `qf`/`ft`/`rn` in the minified bundle; `dev.js` in dev).\n- \"reading 'remove'\" during reconciliation usually means the framework tried to take a DOM node out of a list it no longer holds — the classic causes are two rows sharing a key, or a keyed list being mutated while it draws.\n- **Stack** (prod bundle main-hesa85kj.js):\n\n```\nTypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'remove')\n    at qf (main-hesa85kj.js:1:22637)\n    at ft (main-hesa85kj.js:2:3293)\n    at Object.fn (main-hesa85kj.js:2:3019)\n    at rn (main-hesa85kj.js:1:7545)\n    at y (main-hesa85kj.js:1:7326)\n    at U (main-hesa85kj.js:1:1596)\n    at ft (main-hesa85kj.js:2:3011)\n    at Object.fn (main-hesa85kj.js:1:25143)\n    at rn (main-hesa85kj.js:1:7545)\n    at y (main-hesa85kj.js:1:7326)\n```\n\n- Not yet reproduced on demand.\n- **Next:** a fix PR should first find a reproduction (what was on screen: the chat page, while messages streamed), then bisect the #192–#200 window if the reproduction doesn't point straight at the cause.","created":"2026-08-16T09:33:17-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00","custom":{"pr":"202"}}
{"id":"html-preview-relative-links","parent":"bug-docs","ord":"a0","title":"HTML preview: clicking a relative link to another .html doc does not navigate there #deferral","done":"2026-08-16T17:55:15-04:00","desc":"RULED by the human at #206's gate (2026-08-16), with the example that settles it: folder A holds foo.html and bar.html; foo links to bar; clicking that link must open **bar.html in Olai**.\n\n- The app navigates to bar's own page (URL, sidebar selection, everything) — the same place clicking bar.html in the sidebar lands.\n- What #206 shipped is NOT this: the click swaps the bytes inside the preview frame (the sibling renders sealed, in-frame) while Olai's own page still says foo.html.\n- That in-frame behavior was #206's honest scope; this node is the remaining distance.\n- **Shape of the fix:** the frame's navigation (or a click intercept) tells the host page which vault file it moved to, and the host navigates the app to that document.\n  - Likely a postMessage from the injected prefix script, or intercepting same-vault link clicks before the frame navigates.\n  - Must stay inside the seal's rules: only same-vault .html targets get this treatment; everything else keeps #206's behavior.\n- Needs the e2e scenario the original filing asked for: click a relative link, assert Olai's own page is now bar.html's.\n- **Original filing, for history:** follow-up to #201, whose base made relative links 404 under /media/ — #206 then made them render in-frame; ruled insufficient.","created":"2026-08-16T09:35:51-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00","custom":{"from":"201","pr":"209"}}
{"id":"noderefs-duplicate-target-crash","parent":"bug-tasks","ord":"a2","title":"NodeRefs: a repeated see/after target crashes the page the same way #202 fixed","done":"2026-08-16T12:05:05-04:00","desc":"Found by #202's author while hunting client-draw-crash, deliberately left out of that PR.\n\n- NodeRefs.tsx draws see/after links with `<Key each={props.refs} by=\"id\">` — but an id names the *target*, not the row.\n- A hand-edited .olai repeating a target (`\"see\":[\"x\",\"x\",\"x\"]`), opened at /n/&lt;node&gt;, dies with the identical reconciler stack on the next store frame.\n- Verified against a real server.\n- **RULED** by the human, 2026-08-16: draw ONE — deduplicate at the read.\n  - Matches the write layer's set semantics (a re-add is a silent no-op in plan.ts): a repeated target means one link.\n  - Fix: a dedupe where the refs are read, keeping `by=\"id\"` honest.\n  - Plus its own scenario: a hand-edited duplicate target draws one pill and the page survives.\n- Reproduction and both options are written on PR #202.","created":"2026-08-16T10:21:13-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00","custom":{"pr":"203"}}
{"id":"chat-model-reverts-on-restart","parent":"bug-chat","ord":"a5","title":"Chat: /model choice does not survive an olai restart — the session comes back on sonnet","done":"2026-08-16T22:52:24-04:00","desc":"Reported 2026-08-16: switch the chat to fable with /model, restart olai (new deploy), and the restored chat runs sonnet again.\n\n**ROOT CAUSE — CONFIRMED 2026-08-16.**\n- The deploy container's `~/.claude/settings.json` holds `\"model\": \"sonnet\"` (the human read it out).\n- The pinned adapter (0.66.0, `dist/acp-agent.js` ~5470-5530) picks the model on session/load by priority: (1) `ANTHROPIC_MODEL` env, (2) settings.model, (3) the resumed transcript's live model, (4) default.\n- For a RESUMED session it deliberately RE-ASSERTS an env/settings pin with `query.setModel` (\"a resumed session lands on the transcript's model regardless of env/settings, so the override must be re-asserted\").\n- `/model` is handled inside the wrapped CLI, so the change lives only in the transcript — which the pin then clobbers on every restart.\n\n**IMMEDIATE REMEDY (no code):** delete the `\"model\"` line from the container's `~/.claude/settings.json`.\n- `/model` choices then survive restarts via the transcript, and fresh sessions start on the adapter's default.\n\n**DURABLE FIX (if a settings pin should coexist with /model):**\n- olai remembers the session's chosen model itself and re-applies it after session/load through the model config option.\n- Or upstream: argue the transcript should outrank settings on resume.\n- **Floor either way:** `/model`'s change only becomes visible to olai one turn late (the next turn's init message), because nothing else on the wire carries it.","created":"2026-08-16T11:18:38-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00","custom":{"pr":"212"}}
{"id":"chat-subagent-live-face","parent":"bug-chat","ord":"a6","title":"Chat: a running subagent has no live face — lanes only fill as tool frames arrive","done":"2026-08-17T01:11:57-04:00","desc":"Reported 2026-08-16 with a screenshot: during a fan-out, the panel shows the Agent call as a plain pending dot plus a lane of already-arrived tool rows — nothing says a subagent is running RIGHT NOW.\n\n**It IS possible in ACP:**\n- The pinned adapter streams a subagent's tool calls live, stamped with `parentToolUseId` in `_meta.claudeCode` (exactly what #193's lanes draw), with pending/completed status riding each frame.\n- The e2e suite proves the lane draws them (`the_agent.feature` 82-100).\n\n**What's actually missing**, in the client (`chat/src/agent.ts` ~420-470 and the lane drawing):\n- The Agent frame itself gets no live treatment — a running Task shows the same \"·\" as anything pending: no spinner, no \"running · N calls so far\", no elapsed time.\n- A subagent's TEXT and THINKING are never drawn: `agent_message_chunk` is emitted as \"said\" with the parent meta ignored, so between tool calls a working subagent produces nothing visible.\n  - If the adapter forwards its narration, it would land in the MAIN agent's voice — check whether that interleaving is reachable; that would be its own defect.\n- A subagent spawned but with no first tool call yet has no lane at all — nothing to hang the lane on until a tool frame arrives.\n\n**Fix shape:**\n- Give the Agent frame a running state (derived from its own tool_call status plus the presence of parent-attributed frames since).\n- Decide whether a subagent's narration deserves a collapsed line in its lane (Claude Code's own UI shows \"N tool uses · last: ...\" — a compact live summary, not the full stream).","created":"2026-08-16T11:18:52-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00","custom":{"pr":"214"}}
{"id":"html-preview-scripts-dead","parent":"bug-docs","ord":"a1","title":"HTML preview: the page's own JavaScript does not run — ruled unacceptable; adopt kolu's iframe shape","done":"2026-08-16T13:58:26-04:00","desc":"**Ruled 2026-08-16 by the human:** a previewed .html whose scripts are dead is unacceptable.\n- Today this is by design — the seal (#189, hardened in #197/#201) inlines the document via `srcdoc` with a CSP whose `script-src` allows exactly one hash (the seal's own measure script), so the file's scripts are blocked on purpose.\n- **Overruled:** #189's \"not negotiable\" line — both #197 reviewers had already asked for it to be amended.\n\n**How kolu does it** (the reference, read 2026-08-16): `kolu/packages/solid-fileview/src/renderers/iframe.tsx`.\n- Renders an iframe with `src` pointing at a file-serving route and `sandbox=\"allow-scripts\"` (WITHOUT `allow-same-origin`) — the page's JS runs in an opaque origin: cannot read host cookies/localStorage, CORS-gated fetch from inside is blocked.\n- The route (`kolu/packages/server/src/iframePreviewRoute.ts` + `packages/serve-dir`) serves raw bytes with content-type, guarded per-segment against traversal on the UN-normalized request target.\n- A postMessage bridge is available via ref for host↔frame channels.\n- The sandbox is the boundary; CSP hash-pinning is not part of it.\n\n**The olai shape of that:**\n- Serve the .html body by URL (extend the `/media` route family or a sibling `/preview` route, traversal-guarded like #201's mediaTarget but not picture-only).\n- Switch the frame from `srcdoc` to `src`, keep `sandbox=\"allow-scripts\"` alone.\n\n**Open design points for the PR to argue:**\n- **Privacy promise** (\"a saved page cannot tell anybody else's server what you are reading\"): an opaque origin still loads remote no-cors embeds (img/script src).\n  - If the promise is to survive, the route can send a Content-Security-Policy HEADER permitting inline/own-origin scripts but no remote hosts — JS works, nothing leaves.\n  - If the human would rather drop the promise, that's a deferral to rule.\n- **Measure script** (two-readings height, #197/#201): srcdoc injection dies with srcdoc. Options: inject into the served bytes server-side, a postMessage bridge like kolu's, or read the frame's height another way.\n- **Relative links:** with a real URL base, a relative link navigates INSIDE the frame to the sibling file — this may fix `html-preview-relative-links` for free; say so with a scenario if it does.\n- **Docs:** format.md's seal story and #189's \"not negotiable\" sentence must be rewritten to the new rule.\n\n**Security review non-negotiable on the PR**, as with #197/#201.","created":"2026-08-16T11:22:02-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00","custom":{"pr":"206"}}
{"id":"just-e2e-node-leak","parent":"bug-tests","ord":"a4","title":"just e2e breaks before running a scenario: a system node leaks into the nix e2e shell","done":"2026-08-17T01:51:47-04:00","desc":"Found by #206's author, 2026-08-16, and reproduced on a clean checkout of master — not that PR's doing.\n- `just e2e` fails before a single scenario runs: a system `node` leaks into `nix develop .#e2e` and cannot type-strip @kolu/surface's TypeScript sources under node_modules.\n- **Workaround the author used:** run the suite through `bun ./node_modules/@cucumber/cucumber/bin/cucumber.js` directly.\n- CI's e2e leg is unaffected (green).\n- **Fix direction:** the e2e dev shell should pin/front its own node (or run cucumber under bun) so PATH's node never wins.","created":"2026-08-16T12:15:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00","custom":{"pr":"216"}}
{"id":"done-over-open-work","parent":"bug-tasks","ord":"a1","title":"A done parent must not be able to hide unfinished tasks — gate both doors","done":"2026-08-16T15:26:01-04:00","desc":"Ruled by the human 2026-08-16 after the model-indices slices vanished from the roadmap view.\n\n**Symptom:** the Infrastructure root stored `done`, and done-hiding — correctly, per its own rule that a parent's mark is a claim about the whole branch — hid everything under it, including the four freshly-filed model-indices slices.\n\n**Root cause** (traced through git):\n- Nobody marked it over open children.\n- PR #90 (\"Status is stored, never derived\", 2026-08-11 morning) ended derived parent status and, as its data migration, STAMPED the then-derived rollup into storage — that morning every child under Infrastructure happened to be done, so the derived \"done\" froze onto the root as a stored fact (`\"done\":\"2026-08-11\"`; f69d26d0 reformatted it to an instant the same afternoon).\n- Then five days of new open children accumulated under a root that silently carried done.\n- The mark was true when written and went stale by design: a stored fact over a growing branch, with no constraint at either write.\n- **Sweep of the other roots:** `editor` and `website` also store done but currently hide nothing; `infra`'s mark was cleared in a40583f3.\n\n**The ruling:** this must be a preventable constraint, not a nudge — the history shows one gate is not enough, since the state is reachable through two doors:\n- **set_done over open work**: marking a node done while its SUBTREE holds unfinished tasks (todo/doing — an unmarked bullet is not a task, per #90's own creed, and must not block) is REFUSED, naming the unfinished tasks — the same refusal shape set_doing already has for `after`.\n- **Open work arriving under a done ancestor** — the door this incident actually walked through: add_node with a todo/doing mark, set_todo/set_doing, or a move that lands an unfinished task under a done ancestor. Choose and argue: refuse it, or auto-undo the ancestor's done (louder and kinder to capture flows), but never let it land silently.\n- Web and MCP share the planner, so each gate is written once.\n- Archived subtrees stay exempt as everywhere else.\n- The nudge that set_done currently returns becomes the refusal's message body.","created":"2026-08-16T13:09:12-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00","custom":{"pr":"207"}}
{"id":"agenda-shows-trashed","parent":"bug-dates","ord":"a0","title":"Agenda shows trashed nodes — archived dated work keeps its place on a page about what is owed","done":"2026-08-17T15:18:51-04:00","desc":"**Reported by the human 2026-08-17; RULED same day:** archived (trashed) nodes appear ONLY on the trash page — stripped from the agenda, day pages, and every other page.\n- This reverses the three-archived-doors doctrine #221 documented (trash, day, agenda): trash becomes the sole door.\n- **The fix must sweep:** agendaOf's keep and the \"archive keeps its place\" test (inverted, renamed); day-page collection; #221's Scope.archived (collapses to the trash page alone — the filter exception simplifies); docs/search.md and format README prose.\n- `is:archived` in search remains the explicit way to reach archived nodes from anywhere.\n- Dispatched to Opus.","created":"2026-08-17T08:51:48-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00","custom":{"pr":"226"}}
{"id":"menu-said-overlay","parent":"bug-nav","ord":"a3","title":"MenuSaid still paints under sticky headings — the one overlay #233 left behind #deferral","done":"2026-08-19T20:47:22-04:00","desc":"The findings the human waived when ruling #233 merged without further review (claude reviewer's comment 5322681125, reproduced on the branch).\n\n- **(1)** menu/MenuSaid.tsx — the line carrying the ops layer's refusals — is still `absolute…LAYER.row` in the row, so a sticky section heading paints through it.\n  - The README's stacking table still names it a LAYER.row rider, contradicting overlay.ts's new doctrine.\n- **(2)** the completions half of #233 fixed a second real bug with NO test (fails on master, passes there) and hand-rolls measuring where `@kobalte/core/popper` (already a dep, already anchoring the menu) gives flip/shift/autoUpdate free.\n- **Smaller:** `host.parentElement` fails silently; no claims.test.ts sweep for the new layering rule.","created":"2026-08-18T10:07:11-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00","custom":{"from":"233","pr":"#268 merged a6bd9970 — all three points closed (MenuSaid on overlay.ts, popper adoption, claims sweep)"}}
{"id":"chat-links-reload","parent":"bug-chat","ord":"a7","title":"Chat: a link in the agent's answer full-reloads the app — the transcript answers node chips, not anchors","done":"2026-08-20T11:29:34-04:00","desc":"FOUND by the human after `vault-in-browser` landed (2026-08-20): click a `.md` link in an ACP chat answer and the page reloads from scratch; the same file clicked in the sidebar does not. An audit of every link surface in `packages/web/src/client` found this is the ONE instance — the only internal anchors drawn outside a pane and outside a `<Link>`.\n\n**Why.** The app has exactly two ways an internal link stays in-app: it is a `<Link>` (`router.tsx`), or it is a plain `<a>` inside a pane's `<main>`, whose click bubbles to the pane's delegated listener. The chat panel is mounted BESIDE the panes, and its transcript's only click listener asked one question — `nodeRefIn`, the backtick node-id chips — so every anchor the agent's rendered markdown carried fell through to the browser's default.\n\n**DONE 2026-08-20 — #284 (Opus, merged 1c87295d1; grok do-not-object).** `router.tsx` gained `useFollow`, the one shared tail (`followedSplit` → `openRight`, else `followed` → `go`), called by PageView's listener and the transcript's after its chip check; `useHere` falls back to the focused pane, so a link pressed in the drawer lands where the palette and sidebar land. The fake ACP agent grew a `links` verb; two e2e scenarios click a `.md` link and a `/n/<id>` link (`the page has not reloaded`, the pane shows the target; Alt+click opens to the right). Refactor passes collapsed four wait/click/settle copies in test support onto `world.press(…, modifiers)`. docs/chat.md says it in one sentence.\n- Left for later, filed: `follow-one-unit` — fold `Link` and `Tree.tsx`'s own handler into `useFollow` (every navigation in the app, so not on a bug-fix PR).","see":["external-links-newtab","vault-in-browser"],"created":"2026-08-20T10:30:33-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"regressions","ord":"b00","title":"Regressions","desc":"Behavior that shipped worse than what it replaced, each node naming the offending PR. Ruled into existence 2026-08-15 by the human during the first live one.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00"}
{"id":"stdio-retires","parent":"regressions","ord":"a0","title":"PR: the stdio MCP retires — agents dial the running server over HTTP","done":"2026-08-15T14:54:33-04:00","desc":"RATIFIED 2026-08-15 after the bridge regression's root-cause conversation: one brain, and the door to it is HTTP.\n\n- The `olai mcp` subcommand is DELETED; .mcp.json points at the running server's /mcp route (the user runs `just run`); the ACP chat keeps its self-server MCP unchanged.\n- **Rulings sealed at the door:**\n  - (a) LOOPBACK NEEDS NO TOKEN — requests from 127.0.0.1 skip auth on /mcp, the chat keeps its bearer tokens, same trust stdio had.\n  - (b) The #175 attach/unix-socket machinery goes WITH it — serveOverUnixSocket usage, the dial, OwnedSurfaceConnection wiring, dead code deleted not dormant (the kolu per-face-expose upstream work stays: the web face rides it).\n  - (c) Stable per-repo port so the .mcp.json URL holds — just run binds it.\n- Docs move with it: .mcp.json example, docs/running.md, the charter gains the precondition that unattended agent runs need the server up.\n- This PR obsoleted three nodes filed hours earlier (bridge-no-fallback, socket-litter, mcp-process-leak — all archived with their stories).\n- **ASSIGNED:** Grok, solo, review WAIVED by the human.\n- Fielded to the human at green — merging changes his own session config (.mcp.json → http) and his run habits, so the coordination note rides the fielding.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:42-04:00"}
{"id":"brain-lock","parent":"regressions","ord":"a1","title":"PR: the brain locks its directory — a second olai over the same vault is refused","done":"2026-08-15T16:23:56-04:00","desc":"RATIFIED 2026-08-15, the enforcement half of one-brain.\n\n- **MERGED** the same day (pre-approved on verified evidence): PR #186, packages/server/src/lock.ts.\n  - bun:ffi flock, zero dependencies — the lockfile-family libraries failed the human's own kill-9 requirement (their validity is file-existence plus a staleness window).\n  - Keyed on realpath, pid in the file as DIAGNOSIS only.\n- **Evidence:** the orchestrator verified the transcript by eye.\n  - Second olai refused, naming pid.\n  - Symlinked spelling refused identically.\n  - kill -9 left the lock file on disk and the next boot served anyway — validity is the kernel's.\n- **Review:** Grok + opencode, nothing blocking.\n  - The EINTR disagreement settled IN the docstring with both readings and a bounded retry.\n  - kimi's CodeQL HIGH fixed at the line (0o600).\n- The audit's prediction came true: e2e workers were four olai over one shared fixture vault — per-worker copies now, which also closed a stray-write-into-tracked-fixtures hole.\n- **OPEN FOR THE HUMAN**, reviewers split: LockUnavailable (cannot determine a holder) ships FAIL-CLOSED with no escape.\n  - kimi argued a narrow bypass for only that case (macOS is CI-unproven; a portability miss is a no-dial outage).\n  - grok argued a macOS miss should be a bugfix, not a knob.\n  - Both paths' tests already exist either way.\n- **Cosmetic residue:** the VaultInUse refusal prints inside a raw Effect stack trace rather than as one clean sentence.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:42-04:00"}
{"id":"reactivity-after-the-flip","parent":"regressions","ord":"a2","title":"PR #279: the client stops respecting fine-grained reactivity","done":"2026-08-20T18:14:30-04:00","desc":"After PR #279 the client stops respecting fine-grained reactivity: the sidebar folds and relights on every click, and there are nine other remount sites.\n\nREPORTED by the human, 2026-08-20: a click on a sidebar entry opens the page in the pane (good) but the whole sidebar re-renders and flickers — which says the flip disrespected Solid's fine-grained reactivity. The ask was every such violation, not just this one.\n\n**The audit is `brainstorming/reactivity-after-the-flip.md`** — read it in full before touching anything; it is written so an agent can finish this autonomously: §1 the symptom measured in a browser (16 of 178 sidebar elements destroyed navigating within one folder; 0 across top-level files; the pane remounts with a `Reading…` beat every time), §2 the two framework facts (a kolu stream blanks to `undefined` on every input change; kolu's `reconcile(next, {key:null})` without `merge` replaces every array element per frame — verified against Solid 1.9.14), §3 every finding with `file:line`, severity and a one-line fix, §4 what is already right and must not be touched, §5 the six PRs, §6 the reproduction and the probe that becomes the test.\n\n**The root of the reported symptom**, in one line: `App.tsx:118-212` derives the sidebar's active file, the calendar's open day, the palette's names and undo's file from the focused pane's READING — which blanks for a round trip on every navigation — instead of from the ROUTE, which already knows. Pre-flip it read the route.\n\nThe children are the PRs, in §5's order. PR 1 first (it is the symptom); the rest are independent. The law is `vault-in-browser.md` §6's and HACKING.md's: self-contained PRs, a test per fix, CI green through odu.","see":["vault-in-browser"],"created":"2026-08-20T10:51:13-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T18:14:30-04:00"}
{"id":"reactivity-route-not-reading","parent":"reactivity-after-the-flip","ord":"a0","title":"PR 1: the chrome reads the route, and a navigation swaps the page instead of tearing it down","done":"2026-08-20T12:19:09-04:00","desc":"`brainstorming/reactivity-after-the-flip.md` §3.1 (findings 1.1–1.8) and §5 PR 1.\n- **DONE 2026-08-20 — #285 (Opus, merged e52955f4f; grok do-not-object after re-running the probe itself).** `reading.tsx` holds the last answer across the next question, so `undefined` means only \"this pane was never answered\" and a navigation SWAPS the page instead of tearing it down; `App.tsx` reads `openFile` off `fileNamed(route)` and `openDay` through `requestFor` — the page consulted only for what an address cannot say; `PageView.tsx` gates the FilterBar on `narrowable(route())`; `filter/asking.ts` stops gating its question on the page having rows and asks at once for a query that arrived with an address.\n- Measured (the §6 probe, two client builds, one corpus): sidebar elements destroyed on a within-folder click 11 → 0, three folders deep 37 → 0, a second day of a non-current month 60 → 0 with 144 → 6 sidebar mutations and the month no longer flipping, `aria-current` moving in one observer batch, a `?q=` page drawing one row instead of six-then-one.\n- Tests: four scenarios in `the_chrome_holds_still.feature`, one in `undo.feature`, one line in `pin_to_sidebar.feature` — all six red against master's bundle first. The probe is `packages/tests/support/probe.ts` with reusable steps (`the sidebar did not remount`, `the folder \"…\" stayed open`, `the current mark moved in one frame`, `the month never changed from \"…\"`, `the node \"…\" was never drawn`) for PRs 2–5.\n- Named cost of route-only: a `/#id` that names nothing, and an outline that will not parse, now draw a filter box where they drew none.","created":"2026-08-20T10:51:13-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T12:19:09-04:00"}
{"id":"reactivity-for-by-reference","parent":"reactivity-after-the-flip","ord":"a1","title":"PR 2: nine `<For>`s over wire arrays learn their key — crumbs, referrers, edge chips, prop chips, pins, palette hits, @ rows, header search, refusal lines","done":"2026-08-20T13:18:34-04:00","desc":"`brainstorming/reactivity-after-the-flip.md` §3.2 (2.1–2.10) and §5 PR 2.\n- **DONE 2026-08-20 — #287 (Opus, merged 5c59c7176; grok do-not-object, no findings).** The nine sites take the key the table names — `<Key by=…>` where rows have identity and can move (crumbs, referrers, edge chips, prop chips, pins, palette rows), `<Index>` where positional (the @ menu, the header box, the refusal lines) — in the idiom Shortlist / Completions / NodeRefs / TrashPage already used. 2.10: the names table moved to `names.ts` and holds by value (served.tsx's own arrangement); `namesIn`, two duplicate memos and three copies of the refusal sentence deleted (`refusals.ts`).\n- Measured, the same nine scenarios over two bundles: 4/6 · 3/6 · 3/4 · 8/9 · 16/19 · 22/23 · 5/6 · 22/24 · 1/7 elements destroyed per identical frame on master → 0 everywhere; the filter bar's `role=\"alert\"` line no longer re-announced; the caret stays on the edge panel's × across a write made on disk (master sent it to the body).\n- The region probe joined PR 1's `support/probe.ts` (`markScreen` via `markRegion`) rather than standing beside it.\n- Seen, not touched → filed: `names-table-once` (App.tsx and each pane scan the focused pane's names twice per frame), `one-alert-row` (palette and header box hand-roll the alert row SaidLine draws); 2.11 (Tree.tsx's per-row binding re-runs) is the upstream item.","created":"2026-08-20T10:51:13-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T13:18:34-04:00"}
{"id":"reactivity-equals-guards","parent":"reactivity-after-the-flip","ord":"a2","title":"PR 3: three `equals` and a reset","done":"2026-08-20T14:39:09-04:00","desc":"Three `equals` and a reset — the HTML preview reloads on the other pane's navigation, the composer re-asks per keystroke, the move-to stream never closes.\n- `brainstorming/reactivity-after-the-flip.md` §3.3 (3.1–3.4, 4.7) and §5 PR 3.\n- **DONE 2026-08-20 — #286 (Opus, merged 2326e53c4; grok OBJECTS → addressed → do-not-object).** 3.1: the preview holds while the other pane navigates — /simplify replaced the string key with `useLanding()` in router.tsx (a receptacle 4.9's faces.tsx can reuse); olai-visit 1→2 on master vs unchanged here, proven with side-by-side videos of a tally surviving. 3.2: `subjects` with `equals: sameIds` — nodes.named 23→0 for a typed word with a chip armed. 3.3/3.4: `standing` resets on the said-line's expiry (the moving stream closes; the leaked frame 1→0 by mutation run) and the request is memoed on (record, to) — re-subscriptions 2→0.\n- Grok's one objection (the /simplify pass dropped the open() destinations reset — a second picker asked about the last list) was restored at 427ac38 with a red-first second-picker scenario; move_to_picker 15/15.\n- Disclosed, not this PR's: two local full-suite flakes (the_agent autoscroll under load; zoom_and_navigate scroll restore) proven pre-existing against the merge base.","created":"2026-08-20T10:51:13-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T14:39:09-04:00"}
{"id":"reactivity-per-frame-tax","parent":"reactivity-after-the-flip","ord":"a3","title":"PR 4: the per-frame tax","done":"2026-08-20T14:31:28-04:00","desc":"The per-frame tax: a whole-vault search per frame, two structuredClones of the page per frame for a counter, and six memos without equals.\n- `brainstorming/reactivity-after-the-flip.md` §3.3 (3.5–3.7), §3.4 (4.1–4.6, 4.8) and §5 PR 4.\n- **DONE 2026-08-20 — #290 (Opus, merged 50a2f281a; grok do-not-object, its own clone-probe and wire-count runs).** The page counts its frames off the store (`frames.ts`, a declared stand-in for kolu 5.2): master cloned the whole page twice per frame (≈1,458–1,684 kB on a 2,000-row page) — now zero. Nine memos gained `equals`/`createSelector`/stopped re-deriving; `editing.tsx`'s triple flatten gone; OFF-LIST: `select/selection.ts` flattened the visible tree twice per frame on every page — found by the cleanup pass, fixed, declared.\n- §3.5's coalescer: reproduced (9 whole-vault search.matching per bulk gesture), built both ways, measured 9 → 8, DELETED — no honest client window helps; the `equals` on `matched` landed. The standing cost is `filter-ask-carries-revision` #deferral.\n- What it left the kolu-upstream node: frames.ts retires with 5.2; its walk's 5.1 tripwire is frames.browsertest.ts's third case; a reconnect re-asks one extra match until then.","created":"2026-08-20T10:51:13-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T14:31:28-04:00"}
{"id":"reactivity-small-c","parent":"reactivity-after-the-flip","ord":"a4","title":"PR 5: the C's — five small stale-UI items","done":"2026-08-20T15:49:04-04:00","desc":"The five C's: landing re-scroll on a rewritten file, indent jumps the caret to the end, Enter picks the previous query's row, a sticky `settling`, a last-wins failure slot. `brainstorming/reactivity-after-the-flip.md` §3.4 (4.9–4.13) and §5 PR 5.\n- **DONE 2026-08-20 — #294 (Opus, merged 3a344f8f4; grok do-not-object, ran the scenarios itself).** Four reproduced and fixed with red-on-master scenarios: 4.9 (a reader at 978px stays), 4.10 (\"pick the knobsed\" → \"picked the knobs\"; the caret rule is a rekeys(edit) table beside redraws(edit)), 4.12 (no `see` written to a node typed past; the gate at Shortlist.tsx/completing.tsx, moved by /simplify from take to the KEY — un-swallowing a pointer press on a stale row), 4.13 (browsertest).\n- 4.11 DROPPED: did not reproduce, driven five ways; the audit's §3.4 row now carries the argument (no editor-reachable write leaves this page's reading identical while owing a frame), and redraws.ts's header states the precise version after grok's note.\n- The made decision: a stale Enter spends nothing, silently (dimming rejected as flicker); editing.md says it in the reader's words; a pointer press is never gated.\n- Deferrals filed: `shortlist-row-freshness`, `router-owns-spent-landing` #deferral. Disclosed local-only: serve.test.ts binds 7714 and fails when the production service runs.","created":"2026-08-20T10:51:13-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T15:49:04-04:00"}
{"id":"reactivity-kolu-upstream","parent":"reactivity-after-the-flip","ord":"a5","title":"Upstream (kolu): keyless reconcile and the frame tracker's clones","done":"2026-08-20T18:14:27-04:00","desc":"In kolu: `reconcile` without a key replaces every array element per frame; the frame tracker clones the whole page twice.\n\n`brainstorming/reactivity-after-the-flip.md` §2 Fact B and §3.5; in the kolu repo, then an npins bump here.\n- `@kolu/surface/src/solid/writeValue.ts`: `reconcile(next, {key:null})` with no `merge` — let a stream/collection declare its array key (`key` for rows, `id` for names/crumbs/refs) and `merge: true` for keyless arrays. This is the root of every §3.2 site and of the O(rows)-per-frame binding re-evaluation in `Tree.tsx` (2.11), which has no client-side fix.\n- `createSubscription.ts:306+` `createUpdatedTracker.noteFrame`: two `structuredClone`s + a deep `framesEqual` per frame once any `updated` handler exists — a counting mode that does not clone.\n- Verified against Solid 1.9.14 with the replay in §6 (identical frame → `rows[$TRACK]` and `rows[0].node.title` each notify once today; 0 is the target).\n- After it lands: bump the pin, delete whatever 2.10 / 3.6 had to work around on this side.\n- **What #290 (PR 4) left for this item, 2026-08-20:** `packages/web/src/client/frames.ts` is a declared stand-in for 5.2 — it counts frames off the store and its header says so; when 5.2 lands `createReading` reads the framework's counter and `frames.ts` + `frames.browsertest.ts` go. It also depends on today's `key: null` merge: when 5.1 lands and a stream declares an array key, the walk must descend into array elements — `frames.browsertest.ts`'s third case is the tripwire, deliberately not fixed pre-emptively. And counting off the store drops the tracker's third clause (an equal reconnect snapshot is silent), so a reconnect re-asks one whole-vault match more than it must — 5.2 gives all three clauses back. #287 also left 2.11 and the `equals` on `names.ts` for this item.","created":"2026-08-20T10:51:13-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T18:14:27-04:00","custom":{"pr":"kolu#2190 merged b6378c576; the olai pin-bump half runs as the campaign finale lane"}}
{"id":"redos-acp-diffs","parent":"bug-chat","ord":"a9","title":"Polynomial regex on agent input in acp/diffs.ts #security","done":"2026-08-20T22:20:33-04:00","desc":"CodeQL code-scanning alert 15 (js/polynomial-redos, severity high): relativeTo's cwd.replace(/\\/+$/, \"\") at packages/acp/src/diffs.ts:84 runs on protocol (agent-library) input and scans quadratically on many non-trailing slashes. Fix: linear trim; sweep the chat package's twin trailing-slash trim (named in the doc comment) in the same PR. Dispatched to Grok 2026-08-20 ~21:1x; reviewer opencode; auto-merge on the human's word.","created":"2026-08-20T20:41:34-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:16-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-20 (code-scanning alert)","merge":"pre-approved (auto-merge after review findings + CI)","pr":"#304 merged 23b5b937 — relativeTo counts trailing slashes; alert 15 should close on next default-branch CodeQL analysis (verify)"}}
{"id":"plain-estimate-nested-emphasis","parent":"bug-outline","ord":"a2","title":"Nested bold/italic in a title renders as escaped source #next","done":"2026-08-22T02:22:26-04:00","desc":"- `a **b *c* d** e` in a title falls back to escaped source with a stray `*` — a plainTextEstimate miss in markdown/title.ts.\n- Pre-existing; found while probing #316. Until fixed, #316's refuse-to-highlight fallback is the honest behavior.","created":"2026-08-21T10:20:28-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T02:22:26-04:00","custom":{"from":"#316 review (pre-existing, named so nobody mistakes it for that change)","pr":"#339 merged 7a2a4f62 — the fourteen-regex plainTextEstimate deleted; the loss check's source side is mdast-util-to-string over markdown's own parse behind the render door; nested emphasis in every spelling, tag/link neighbours and `Tom &amp; Jerry` render; the refusal rule unchanged; 3 assumptions for the human (picture-in-title still falls back; one-directional length check as on master; mdast-util-to-string defaults)"}}
{"id":"e2e-log-truncation-flake","parent":"bug-tests","ord":"a5","title":"e2e CI red is still un-diagnosed — the log class that hid it is FIXED upstream","todo":true,"desc":"- Defect (b) — the log-delivery truncation — is FIXED: odu#89 (3d0db227, 2026-08-21) moved #88's status-to-log join from teardown to the verdict gate after twelve-plus sightings; a red log now carries its tail and its summary.\n- Defect (a) remains OPEN: the rare real e2e failure (three first-attempt reds on #327's branch, never named — the old truncation destroyed every diagnosis). Nothing to do but observe: the NEXT red e2e log will finally carry the failing scenario's name — capture it here when it appears.\n- History: sightings #296(3×) #309 #313 #317 #318 #321(3×) #322 #327(3×) #328 across ≥4 hosts; the forensics that cracked it (settled:true with the file completing 25s later) are on odu#89.","created":"2026-08-21T11:39:22-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T20:25:04-04:00","custom":{"from":"orchestrator pattern-match 2026-08-21; sightings: #296 (3×), #309, #313, #317, #318, #321 (3×), #322 (passing run), #328, #327 (3× consecutive, ACTIVELY BLOCKING diagnosis — the truncation is hiding a possibly-real failure exactly as the node predicted) — twelve-plus occurrences; the odu drain fix is now urgent and awaits the human's cross-repo ratification","upstream-fix":"odu#89 merged 3d0db227"}}
{"id":"manifest-fold-skew","parent":"bug-server","ord":"a9","title":"The error page can show while file paths are already loaded #next","done":"2026-08-22T02:08:11-04:00","desc":"- Pre-existing skew found by #317's review: Directory.manifest can still be null (drawing the error page) while the fold has already seeded — live paths hidden behind the error page.\n- Lives in runtime.ts's tolerate-the-skew window. Small, real.","created":"2026-08-21T12:00:18-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T02:08:11-04:00","custom":{"from":"#317 review (grok's leak hunt; pre-existing, outlives that branch)","pr":"#338 merged 950d7625 — Directory.manifest → Directory.standing ('reading'|'never'|'loaded') resolved from the cell AND the fold in the one place both are held; both skew orders handled; wire untouched; cross-package invariant pinned server-side; the skew driver committed as packages/tests/skew.ts; 3 assumptions for the human (paths outrank a stale null; the rename in scope; no cucumber scenario for the window)"}}
