{"id":"calendar-click-mints","parent":"bug-dates","ord":"a1","title":"Clicking an empty calendar day silently creates a document","done":"2026-08-21T20:43:33-04:00","desc":"- Today a day cell has two meanings behind one gesture: a day with content links to /d/&lt;date&gt;, but an EMPTY day click mints that day's note and lands in its editor (Calendar.tsx:101, Day.tsx:180). A navigation gesture writes a file — and a day cell is the smallest click target in the app, so a misclick creates a document to trash.\n- Worse, the calendar cell is the ONLY mint site: a day that already has entries links to the day view, which offers no way to create that day's note at all.\n\n**Fix (ruled):**\n- Clicking ANY day always navigates to /d/&lt;date&gt;. An empty day shows the honest empty state (\"nothing dated this day\").\n- The day page gains an explicit \"+ day note\" button, shown on any day without a note — entries or not.\n- The creation code is reused unchanged: the docDay verb (server reads the vault's daily-note convention), mintAndOpen into the editor, the undo record, the verbatim refusal. Only the trigger moves from the calendar cell to the button.","created":"2026-08-21T19:16:34-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T20:43:33-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-21 (UX review of the calendar click)","pr":"#333 merged e9640603 — every day cell navigates, the honest empty state, minting explicit via + day note on the day page (DayMint.tsx), creation code trigger-moved unchanged"}}
{"id":"new-file-bare-name","parent":"bug-nav","ord":"a4","title":"+ New outline / + New document refuse a bare name: `Foo` should mint Foo.olai (and Foo.md), `Foo.olai` still accepted #next","done":"2026-08-22T03:58:32-04:00","desc":"- Sidebar `+ New outline`, type `Foo`, Enter → the box shows the ops layer's refusal verbatim: \"`Foo` is not a relative `.olai` path under the served directory (no absolute path, no `..`, no `.`, and the name must end in `.olai`)\" — instead of creating `Foo.olai`. Same door, same defect for `+ New document` and `.md` (one box serves both: web/src/client/file/NewFile.tsx + making.ts; the refusal is plan.ts's create_outline / create_document validation).\n- **Ruled:** the box accepts BOTH `Foo` and `Foo.olai` (`Foo.md` for the document door) — a bare name takes the door's own suffix; a name already carrying it is taken as is; a name carrying the OTHER suffix (`Foo.md` typed into the outline door) is the one honest refusal left, said in the box's own words. Paths with folders (`notes/plan`) get the same treatment.\n- Where: the client completes the name before asking the ops layer (the door KNOWS its kind — `Making.of`), so the ops contract stays strict and one spelling; the placeholder/aria can say the suffix is optional. The refusal that remains must be the box's sentence, not the wire's paragraph.","created":"2026-08-21T22:07:28-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T03:58:32-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-21 ~22:05, with a screenshot: typed Foo into + New outline, got the ops layer's path refusal","pr":"#340 merged 6b464c99 — the box completes a bare name with the door's suffix (Foo → Foo.olai / Foo.md, notes/plan → notes/plan.olai), takes Foo.olai as is, refuses the other kind's suffix in its own words, and passes `.`/`..`/trailing-separator texts through to the planner's paragraph; MCP contract untouched; 3 assumptions for the human (Foo.txt → Foo.txt.olai; Foo. completes, .. does not; the sentence's wording)","ruled":"the human: the box accepts both `Foo` and `Foo.olai`, naturally — queued into the overnight campaign (lane-nob)"}}
{"id":"markdown-raw-flash","parent":"bug-docs","ord":"a2","title":"Markdown flashes as RAW SOURCE for a moment before it renders — documents, notes, titles, chat, palette rows #needs-brainstorm #now","todo":true,"desc":"**The glitch.** A `.md` page (and every other markdown surface) paints its escaped SOURCE first and swaps to rendered HTML a moment later. It is written down as intended (\"raw text now, rendered a moment later\" — Markdown.tsx, chunk.ts): the remark+rehype pipeline is a lazy chunk (~95 KB brotli) fetched the first time something on the page asks, and while `markdownReady()` is false the component draws the file's own text `pre-wrap`, chosen over a blank or a spinner. Two consequences: (1) on a first visit / after a deploy the marks are visible for the fetch's duration; (2) even with the chunk cached (immutable asset) there is still at least one painted frame of source, because the first synchronous render happens before the dynamic `import()` resolves. So it is structural, not a timing accident.\n\n**Where it happens** — every caller of render.ts's guarded entry points: a tree row whose title has markdown (plain titles skip the pipeline via plain.ts), the ¶ notes, the day page's note, the document body / previews / referrers, agent messages in the chat panel, palette and search hits with markdown titles.\n\n**Fix shapes, for the brainstorm** (the human: progress feedback on loading pages is probably part of it):\n1. Route-level readiness — a page whose content is markdown-first (document, day-with-note, chat) waits for the chunk under ONE boundary before its first paint, with honest progress feedback (the page says it is loading, never shows source); outlines still paint without it; `modulepreload` the pipeline chunk from the shell so the wait is ~0 after the first visit.\n2. Fold the pipeline back into the main bundle — +95 KB brotli on first paint, cached thereafter, zero flash everywhere; simplest.\n3. Never draw source — hold the previous rendering or a height-preserving placeholder while waiting (still a blank blink on first load without feedback).\nWhatever the shape: one rule for all the surfaces above, and a scenario that pins \"no frame of raw markdown is ever painted\" (the `data-markdown=\"waiting\"` attribute already names the state).","created":"2026-08-22T07:30:10-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-22 ~07:40 — saw a .md page arrive as raw text, then become HTML a split second later","ruled":"the human: file it for NOW; the fix needs brainstorming and will probably involve progress feedback on loading pages","where":"packages/web/src/client/markdown/Markdown.tsx (innerHTML = html() ?? escapeHtml(source)), render.ts's guarded entry points, chunk.ts's lazy import; callers: NodeTitle.tsx, Note.tsx, day/DayNote.tsx, document/DocumentPage.tsx + faces.tsx + DocRef.tsx, chat/Entry.tsx, palette/items.ts, search/row.ts + Result.tsx"}}
{"id":"opencode-send-silent","parent":"bug-chat","ord":"aA","title":"A turn that ends having said nothing is drawn as nothing — opencode's auth failure comes back as an empty end_turn","done":"2026-08-22T11:50:44-04:00","desc":"- Reported 2026-08-22 on the deployed server (kolu-bot, user toor) right after #336: pick opencode, send a message — the row appears, then nothing. Header `opencode  Juspay/kimi-k3  0/256k`. Journal: zero chat lines.\n- **Why opencode failed there (deployment, not olai code):** its config reads the LiteLLM key as `\"apiKey\": \"{env:JUSPAY_API_KEY}\"`, and the olai systemd user unit's environment carries only PATH — the opencode olai spawns has no key. Fix: `systemd.user.services.olai.Service.EnvironmentFile` (or an HM `environmentFile` option) holding the key; docs/running.md should say an agent olai spawns inherits the SERVER's environment, not your shell's. (The `opencode run` error on that host — `no such column: replacement_seq` — is an unrelated opencode CLI-path bug.)\n- **Why olai drew nothing — REPRODUCED locally, pixel-identical to the report (screenshots in the session scratchpad):** with a broken provider key, opencode 1.17.9 does NOT return a JSON-RPC error through the ACP client: it sends `available_commands_update`, then `usage_update {used:0,size:256000}`, then answers `session/prompt` with a SUCCESSFUL `{stopReason:\"end_turn\", usage: 0 tokens}`. No message chunk, no error. (A direct driver on the host once got `-32603 No api key passed in` instead — that shape IS drawn: chat.ts:1018 publishes the notice unconditionally, traced end to end. The silent end_turn is the one that matches the screen.)\n- **The mechanism in chat.ts:** the success branch has NO arm for \"the turn succeeded and the agent said nothing\" — `outcome` is `Success(\"end_turn\")` (chat.ts:1000), settle (1016), the only check is `=== \"cancelled\"` (1051), then `move({status:\"idle\", trouble:null})` (1057). The `heard`/`quietSince` evidence (996/1030) lives only inside the Failure branch. And `\"usage\"` is in SPOKE (275-280), so a zero-token usage frame counts as \"the agent worked on it\" — which is exactly the case where it didn't.\n\n**Fix:**\n1. In the success branch, before going idle: if nothing a person can see arrived this turn (no `said`, no `tool`, no `asked` — a narrower set than SPOKE; `usage` alone is the auth-failure signature), publish a notice row (\"the agent finished without saying anything — check its provider key / `opencode auth login`\") and leave `trouble` set. Honest for every agent, free on a normal turn.\n2. Drop `usage` from the evidence that suppresses `markUndelivered` (split SPOKE: what-a-person-can-see vs has-anything-arrived for cancel), so a -32603 after a zero-token usage frame still marks the row unsent with send-again.\n3. A running turn gets a visible busy face (the composer's orange border is focus styling only).\n4. Pin with a scripted opencode-shaped agent answering `end_turn` + a lone `usage_update`.\n- Logging is chat-lifecycle-logs.","created":"2026-08-22T07:36:17-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T11:50:44-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-22, on the deployed instance after #336","pr":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/343 — merged 2026-08-22 as a314683c"}}
{"id":"chats-list-per-agent","parent":"bug-chat","ord":"aB","title":"The chats list shows only the current agent's conversations — Claude's vanish after an opencode chat","done":"2026-08-22T11:50:45-04:00","desc":"- With Claude and opencode both installed: create one opencode chat and the \"chats\" list shows only opencode sessions; every Claude conversation is gone from view until you create a NEW Claude chat just to see them.\n- **Mechanism (verified):** `chat.ts:1351` `sessions: onAgent(agent => agent.sessions)` — `onAgent` resolves `talking`, the one chosen agent; `agent.ts:941-955` `storedFor` sends `session/list` on the single running child and filters to the cwd. The roster already knows every installed agent (`agents/roster.ts:151,168`), but only the chosen row is ever spawned.\n- **Fix:** `chat.sessions` fans out over `roster()` rather than `talking`: ask each installed agent's `session/list` (spawning lazily, or a cached answer with a short TTL so opening the list doesn't start three subprocesses), tag each `SessionInfo` with its agent id (one added wire field), merge newest-first. `Sessions.tsx` groups by agent with its icon; picking a row from another agent switches the panel to that agent the way `newSession` already does. One-agent-at-a-time stays true at the process level, not at the list.","created":"2026-08-22T07:36:17-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T11:50:45-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-22, on the deployed instance after #336","pr":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/343 — merged 2026-08-22 as a314683c"}}
{"id":"send-during-boot-doubles","parent":"bug-chat","ord":"aC","title":"A message sent while a freshly picked agent is still booting can be delivered twice","done":"2026-08-22T11:50:46-04:00","desc":"- Reproduced (shots in the session scratchpad): pick an agent, type and send before the boot settles — two identical user rows and two agent answers.\n- **Mechanism:** `deliver`'s permit (chat.ts ~815) serializes deliveries against each other but not against the `opening()` permit in agent.ts:1384; a send landing in the newSession window races the open and produces two full turns. The client also reports `idle` for the first frames after `surface/chat/newSession` goes out (the panel isn't `booting` yet when the click lands).\n- **Fix:** `+ new` / the picker flips the panel to `booting` synchronously on the click, and the server's `send` takes the same permit `opening` holds, so a prompt typed during a boot queues behind exactly one open instead of racing it. Pin with a scenario that sends during the boot window.","created":"2026-08-22T07:56:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T11:50:46-04:00","custom":{"from":"found by the 2026-08-22 repro of opencode-send-silent","pr":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/343 — merged 2026-08-22 as a314683c"}}
{"id":"inbox-count-counts-done","parent":"bug-nav","ord":"a5","title":"The Inbox badge counts done rows — says 3 over an inbox that draws empty","done":"2026-08-22T17:10:52-04:00","desc":"- `inboxHeldOf` (format/src/inbox.ts:80) counts `rootsOf(derived, file).length` — every top-level node of the inbox, marks ignored. A processed (done) row keeps inflating the badge while the page shows nothing, so the door says 3 over an empty room.\n- **Fix (the human's ruling):** the count is what still awaits processing — top-level rows NOT marked done. A bullet or a todo/doing counts; a done row doesn't. One filter in `inboxHeldOf`, its unit test beside it, and the badge agrees with the page again.","created":"2026-08-22T12:32:28-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T17:10:52-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-22 (screenshot: Inbox badge 3, page empty; the 3 were done)","pr":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/348 — merged 2026-08-22 as 6491980b"}}
{"id":"inbox-count-headers","parent":"inbox-count-counts-done","ord":"a0","title":"The Inbox badge still says 1 over a finished branch — a bare-bullet HEADER whose children are all done is not \"awaiting processing\"","done":"2026-08-22T17:10:52-04:00","desc":"#348 made `inboxHeldOf` count top-level rows whose stored mark is not `done` — and \"a bullet counts\". The Inbox's `Deferrals` root is a bare-bullet header with 10/10 done children: it counts as 1 while nothing under it awaits processing, and the page shows exactly that finished branch. The rule needs one more clause: a top-level bullet WITH children counts only if some descendant is unfinished (todo/doing, or a bullet leaf); a leaf bullet still counts; a branch whose every task is done does not. Done-marked roots stay excluded as today; mirrors/placements stay excluded. One filter in `inboxHeldOf`, unit tests beside it (finished branch → not counted; branch with one todo → counted; leaf bullet → counted), the docs that state the rule updated (docs/editing.md, docs/format.md, packages/format/README.md and the surface/web READMEs that #348 touched).","created":"2026-08-22T16:15:00-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T17:10:52-04:00","custom":{"dispatch":"resume the same Grok session that shipped #348 (grok --continue in .worktrees/inbox-count-counts-done); opencode reviewer; auto-merge on verification","from":"the human 2026-08-22 16:30 (screenshot: Inbox badge 1; the page shows only `Deferrals ¶ 10/10`); ruled the same minute: a bullet with children counts only if something under it is unfinished; a leaf bullet still counts; a finished branch doesn't","pr":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/351 — merged 2026-08-22 as 2de9cd19"}}
{"id":"runtime-dir-flood","parent":"bug-tests","ord":"a6","title":"Test servers leak lock files and keep running #now","doing":true,"desc":"Found 2026-08-23 on the human's machine: `/run/user/1000/olai/` holds 163,765 files (151,369 `.lock` from the one-server-per-vault lock, #186; 12,396 `.sock` from the old `olai mcp` rendezvous socket, #175, retired the same day by #184) — 592 MB, growing since Aug 15, one per scratch vault the tests ever started. And 230 `olai web` processes from Aug 21–22 are still running on directories that no longer exist.\n\nFix, in one PR:\n1. A server removes its lock file when it stops (the \"bun --watch needs it\" excuse applies only to the dev loop — keep it only there).\n2. On start, a server sweeps the runtime directory: any `.lock` whose pid is dead or whose root is gone, and any `.sock`, is deleted (the lock file already records both pid and root).\n3. The e2e harness owns the servers it starts: they die with the run (process group / kill on exit), and `olai web` exits on its own when its root directory disappears.\nEvidence: the before count on this machine, the after count, a transcript of a cancelled e2e run leaving nothing behind.","created":"2026-08-23T12:12:23-04:00","changed":"2026-08-23T12:23:19-04:00","custom":{"from":"orchestrator RCA 2026-08-23 while chasing the wrong-vault capture; the human: its own lane, Grok now, opencode reviewer","ruled":"the human 2026-08-23 12:30: its own lane, spawned by Grok right now, opencode reviewer; the PR waits for the human's approval","where":"packages/server/src/lock.ts (the `<digest>.lock` in runtimeHome()), serve.ts:398 (not unlinked on teardown), the e2e harness's serve spawning (packages/tests)"}}
